hadiths[553]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","631 - And Ibn al-Tabba', Nu'aym, and Ibrahim ibn Hamzah said: from Yahya, as Mahmud said it."
"602","632 - And al-Nufayli said: from Yahya ibn Sulaym, from Isma'il, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"603","633 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of dogs and cats."
"604","634 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of dogs, the dowry of prostitutes, and the fee of soothsayers."
"605","635 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Ibn Ulayyah, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the stallion's semen."
"606","636 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of the cupper, and he forbade him it, but he complained of their need, so he said: Feed your camel with it, and feed your slaves with it."
"607","637 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn and Hisham both informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"608","638 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the briber and the bribed."
"609","639 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abdillah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the briber and the bribed."
"610","640 - Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slavewomen."
"611","641 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Mutawakkil narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped among a tribe of the Arabs, but they did not host them nor entertain them as guests. The chief (of the tribe) was stung, so they came to us and said: Do you have a remedy? We said: Yes, but you did not host us nor entertain us, so we will not do it unless you assign us a wage. So they assigned them for that a flock of sheep. A man among us began reciting the Fatihat al-Kitab over him, and when they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we mentioned that to him. He said: How did you know that it is a ruqyah? And he did not mention any prohibition from him. Then he said: Eat, and assign for me a share with you in the wage."
"612","642 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a camel from me, and he weighed out its price for me and gave me extra."
"613","Chapter 65: On prohibited transactions involving uncertainty (gharar) and other matters. 643 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Umar - narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar (uncertainty) and the sale of pebbles (hasah)."
"614","644 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of habal al-habalah (the offspring of an unborn animal)."
"615","645 - Ibn al-Muqri and Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales and two ways of wearing: as for the two sales, they are mulamasah (touch sale) and munabadhah (throw sale); and as for the two ways of wearing, they are wrapping in one garment (ishtimal al-samma') and sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it covering his private parts."
"616","646 - Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sayyar, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not trade by throwing pebbles, and do not engage in najsh, and do not trade by mulamasah (touch). Whoever among you buys a muhaffalah (an animal whose milk was retained) and dislikes it, let him return it along with a sa' of food."
"617","647 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, that he heard Abu al-Minhal saying: I heard Iyas ibn Abd al-Muzani saying: Do not sell water, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the sale of water. I do not know which water it is. And Sufyan said another time: Abu al-Minhal informed him."
"618","648 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of surplus water."
"619","649 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not to be withheld so that herbage may thereby be withheld. Sufyan said: And there are three that are not withheld: water, herbage, and fire."
"620","650 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit years in advance."
"621","651 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man and Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr and Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, mukhabarah, and mu'awamah. The other said: the sale of years, and (he forbade) thunya (exceptions), and he permitted arayah."
"622","652 - Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The delay of the rich is injustice, and if you are transferred to a solvent person then follow him, and do not sell two sales in one."
"623","653 - Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade two sales in one sale."
"624","654 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us that Isma'il ibn Ulayyah informed them, from Ayyub, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, until he mentioned Abdillah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A loan combined with a sale is not lawful, nor two conditions in a sale, nor profit on what is not guaranteed, nor the sale of what is not with you."
"625","655 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Fadalah al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ya'la - that is Ibn Hakim - he said: Yusuf ibn Mahak narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Ismah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who buys sales, so what of them is lawful and what is unlawful? He said: O son of my brother, if you buy a sale, do not sell it until you have taken possession of it."
"626","656 - And thus said Shayban and Hammam, from Yahya, from Ya'la, from Yusuf, from Abdillah ibn Ismah, from Hakim. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Shayban."
"627","657 - And Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Habban narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us."
"628","658 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit until their soundness appears."
"629","659 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sale of palm trees is not valid until their soundness appears. They said: And what is its soundness? He said: They turn red and yellow."
"630","660 - Ali ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ulayyah - narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of palm trees until they blossom, and (forbade the sale) of grain until it whitens and is safe from blight; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."
"631","661 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: What the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade is food being sold until it is taken possession of. Ibn Abbas said: And I do not consider anything but the same."
"632","662 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We used to buy food from the riders in bulk, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to sell it until we moved it from its place."
"633","663 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of a pile of dates whose measure is unknown for measured dates."
"634","664 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit."
"635","665 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shihab - meaning Ibn Abbad - narrated to us, he said: Dawud - meaning al-Attar - narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that an animal be sold for an animal on credit."
"636","666 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit."
"637","667 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that Safiyyah fell in the share of Dihyah al-Kalbi, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought her for seven heads."
"638","668 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a slave for two black slaves."
"639","Chapter 67: On salam (advance payment). 669 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Najih, from Abdillah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina while they were advancing payment for fruits for two and three years, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advance payment for fruits should be in a known measure to a known term."
"640","670 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdillah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina while they were advancing payment for fruits for two and three years, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advance payment for fruits should be in a known measure and a known weight."
"641","671 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Mujalid, he said: Abdillah ibn Shaddad and Abu Burdah disputed about salam, so they sent me to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa and I asked him, and he said: We used to advance payment at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the time of Abu Bakr and the time of Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, for wheat, barley, raisins, and dates, to people who did not have it with them. 672 - He said: Then I asked Ibn Abza, and he said the same."
"642","Chapters on judgment in sales. 673 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two sellers have the option as long as they have not parted, or their sale is with an option."
"643","674 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me that Nafi' narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two men trade, each of them has the option as long as they have not parted and were together, or one of them gives the other the option, and they trade on that, then the sale has become binding; and if they part after trading and neither of them has abandoned the sale, then the sale has become binding."
"644","675 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Jamil ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi, he said: We went on one of our expeditions and camped at a station, and a companion of ours sold a horse to a man for a slave, and they remained the rest of their day and their night until morning. When the time of departure came, the man went to his horse to saddle it and regretted, so the (other) man held him to the sale, and they came to Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, and told him their story. He said: Do you accept that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the option as long as they have not parted."
"645","676 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Mas'adah - narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seller and the buyer have the option as long as they have not parted, except in an option bargain, and it is not lawful for him to leave him fearing that he will rescind."
"646","677 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Qurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys a musarrat has the option for three days, and if he returns it he returns with it a sa' of food, not samra'. Abu Amir said: meaning: not wheat."
"647","678 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever woman is married by two guardians belongs to the first, and whichever man sells a sale to two men, the sale belongs to the first."
"648","679 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If two agents sell, the sale belongs to the first, and if two guardians marry, the marriage belongs to the first."
"649","680 - Abu Zur'ah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: Abdillah ibn Mas'ud sold al-Ash'ath ibn Qays captives from the captives of the leadership for twenty thousand, and he came to him with ten thousand, and he said: I sold you for twenty thousand. He said: I took them for ten thousand. He said: I accept in that your opinion. Ibn Mas'ud said: If you wish I shall narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I will do so. He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If two traders trade a sale with no witnesses between them, the word is what the seller says, or they rescind the sale. Al-Ash'ath said: I have returned it to you."
"650","681 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abu Umays, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: al-Ash'ath bought slaves from the slaves of the khumus (fifth) from Abdillah for twenty thousand, and Abdillah sent to him about their price, and he said: I took them for ten thousand. Abdillah said: Choose a man to be between me and you. Al-Ash'ath said: You are between me and myself. Abdillah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If the two sellers differ and there is no proof between them, then it is as the owner of the goods says, or they rescind."
"651","682 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Shafi'i, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that a man bought a slave and used him, then a defect appeared in him, so he disputed about him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he judged that he return him. The seller said: O Messenger of Allah, he has taken his yield. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yield belongs with liability."
"652","683 - Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, he said: Makhlad ibn Khufaf narrated to me, from Urwah, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Yield belongs with liability."
"653","684 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sells pollinated palm trees, its fruit belongs to the one who sold it, unless the buyer stipulates."
"654","685 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the one who sold him, unless the buyer stipulates."
"655","686 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that he informed him that he heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrating, that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrating, that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes bankrupt with the wealth of people, and a man finds his goods intact with him, he has more right to them than others."
"656","687 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khabayiri narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whichever man sells goods and then finds his goods intact with a man who has gone bankrupt, and he has not received anything of its price - then it is his; but if he had received something of its price, then what remains, he shares with the creditors."
"657","688 - Ibn Awf narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same, and he added: And whichever man dies while another man's wealth is intact with him, whether he received something of it or not, he shares with the creditors."
"658","689 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning bankruptcy. 690 - Ibn Yahya said: Malik, Salih ibn Kaysan, and Yunus narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr, without attribution to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they are more entitled to the hadith, meaning: from the path of al-Zuhri."
"659","691 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Abi Fudayk informed them, he said: And Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Mu'tamir ibn Amr narrated to me, from Ibn Khaldah al-Zuraqi, who was the judge of Medina, he said: We came to Abu Hurayrah about a companion of ours who had gone bankrupt, and he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged: Whichever man dies or goes bankrupt, the owner of the goods has more right to his goods if he finds them intact."
"660","692 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I sold a camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I stipulated its riding back to my family."
"661","693 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell me your camel. He said: I said: No, rather it is yours. He said: Sell it to me. I said: So-and-so owes me an ounce of gold, so it is yours for it. Then he took it and said: Ride it to your family. When I arrived, he ordered Bilal to pay me, and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"662","694 - Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan - meaning Ibn Hamzah, his uncle - narrated to me, from Kathir - meaning Ibn Zayd - from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muslims are bound by their conditions as long as they agree with the truth."
"663","695 - Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan - meaning Ibn Hamzah - narrated to me, from Kathir, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Settlement is permissible among Muslims."
"664","696 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, that Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki informed him, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you sell dates to your brother and they are struck by a calamity, it is not lawful for you to take anything from him; for what would you take your brother's wealth without right?"
"665","697 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waived calamities (losses in crops)."
"666","Chapter 68: What has come concerning preemption (shuf'ah). 698 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever among you has land or palm trees, let him not sell it until he has offered it to his partner."
"667","699 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abdillah - meaning Ibn Idris - informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged preemption in every undivided partnership, whether land or wall; it is not lawful for him to sell until he informs his partner; if he wishes he takes, and if he wishes he leaves; but if he sells without informing him, he has more right to it."
"668","700 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made preemption only in what has not been divided; when the boundaries fall and the roads are arranged, there is no preemption."
"669","701 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The neighbor has more right to the house or land of his neighbor."
"670","702 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la ibn Ka'b al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-Sharid narrating, from al-Sharid. He said: And Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father - and this is the hadith of Abu Asim - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to his saqab. Abu Nu'aym added: He said: I said to Amr: What is his saqab? He said: Preemption. I said: People claim it is proximity? He said: People say that."
"671","Chapter 69: What has come concerning riba. 703 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba, its feeder, its two witnesses, and its writer, and said: They are equal."
"672","704 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami and Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, they said: al-Nadr - that is Ibn Muhammad - narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah - meaning Ibn Ammar - narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Riba has seventy gates, the lightest of them with Allah is like one who marries his mother."
"673","705 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Abdillah al-Za'farani, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silver for silver and gold for gold, equal for equal; whoever gives more or takes more has committed riba; the taker and the giver are equal."
"674","706 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Men of knowledge informed me, among them Malik ibn Anas, that Nafi', the freedman of Ibn 'Umar, narrated to them, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some, and do not sell silver for silver except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some, and do not sell anything of it absent for present."
"675","707 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadh-dha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt - like for like, hand to hand; but if these kinds differ, then sell as you wish, provided it is hand to hand."
"676","708 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, he said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for silver is riba except on the spot, and dates for dates is riba except on the spot, and wheat for wheat is riba except on the spot, and barley for barley is riba except on the spot."
"677","709 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir al-Ahmasi, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him. And Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Marwan - meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him - and this is his hadith from Waki' - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for gold, pan for pan, and silver for silver, pan for pan, until he specified salt. 'Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, I do not care not to be in the land of Mu'awiyah. And Marwan said: Until he specified mentioning salt."
"678","710 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to be given inferior dates in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would sell two sa's for one sa', so that was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: No two sa's of dates for one sa', and no two dirhams for one dirham."
"679","711 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me that he heard 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi saying: I heard Fadalah ibn 'Ubayd al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a necklace containing beads and gold while he was at Khaybar, and it was from the spoils being sold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the gold in the necklace be removed by itself, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Gold for gold, weight for weight."
"680","712 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi', so I would sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars. He said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Hafsah, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, wait a moment, I ask you! I sell camels at al-Baqi', and I sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars. He said: There is no harm, if you take them at the rate of the day, as long as you do not part while anything remains between you."
"681","713 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of dates until their ripeness appears, and forbade the sale of fruit for fruit."
"682","714 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas and Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from 'Abdillah ibn Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, that Abu 'Ayyash, the freedman of Banu Zuhrah, informed him that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about buying dates with fresh dates, and he said: Does the fresh date decrease when it dries? They said: Yes, so he forbade it."
"683","715 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted 'araya to be sold by its estimate in measure."
"684","716 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik informed me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, that Abu Sufyan, the freedman of Ibn Abi Ahmad, informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of 'araya for less than five awsuq, or in five awsuq. Dawud ibn al-Husayn doubted: he did not know whether five awsuq or less than five."
"685","717 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Yazid - meaning Ibn Harun - informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the 'ariyyah to be taken for its like by estimate as dates, which its people eat as fresh dates."
"686","718 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with Khaybar for half of what comes out of it, of dates or crops."
"687","719 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: 'Uqbah narrated to me, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs, eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley. When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, rose, he divided Khaybar, and gave the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the choice to have land allocated to them or to guarantee them the wasqs; some of them chose to have land allocated, and some chose the wasqs. And 'A'ishah and Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with them both, were among those who chose the wasqs."
"688","720 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled the Jews from the land of the Hijaz; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prevailed over Khaybar, wanted to expel the Jews from it, and the land when he prevailed over it belonged to Allah and to His Messenger and to the Muslims, and he wanted to expel the Jews from it, so the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to leave them in it on condition that they undertake its work, with half the dates for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: We leave you in it on that as long as we wish. So they remained in it until 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled them to Tayma' and Ariha'."
"689","721 - 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought food from a Jew and pawned to him an iron armor."
"690","722 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Zakariyya - meaning Ibn Abi Za'idah - from 'Amir, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A back is ridden in return for its upkeep when it is pawned, and the milk of a milch animal is drunk when it is pawned, and the upkeep is upon the one who drinks and rides."
"691","Chapter 70: The chapter of found property and strays. 723 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas and 'Amr ibn al-Harith and Sufyan ibn Sa'id al-Thawri and others informed me that Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to them, from Yazid, the freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I was with him, and asked about found property, so he said: Know its container and its string, then announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise do with it as you wish. He said: And a stray sheep? He said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: And a stray camel? He said: With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees, until its master meets it."
"692","724 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan. He said: And 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, the freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: A Bedouin asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about found property, and he said: Announce it for a year; if someone comes to you informing you of its container and its string, otherwise enjoy it. And he asked him about a stray camel? So his face changed color, and he said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees; leave it until its master meets it. And he asked him about a stray sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. This is the hadith of al-Firyabi."
"693","725 - 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, he said: I found a whip and took it, so Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabi'ah disapproved of that to me, so I said: If I find its owner I will hand it to him, otherwise I will enjoy it. He said: So I mentioned that to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: You did well, you did well; I found a purse and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Announce it; so I announced it for a year, and found no one who knew it, so he said: Know its number, its vessel, and its string; if its owner comes, hand it to him, otherwise enjoy it."
"694","726 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about found property, and he said: Announce it for a year; if it is not claimed, then know its container and its string, then consume it; but if its owner comes, hand it to him."
"695","727 - Ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith and Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from 'Abdillah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man from Muzaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think about what is found on a traveled road, and in an inhabited village? He said: Announce it for a year; if its seeker comes, hand it to him, otherwise do with it as you wish; but if its seeker comes one day, hand it to him. And what is on an untraveled road, or in an uninhabited village, then in it and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"696","728 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Khalid al-Hadh-dha', from Yazid ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever picks up a found thing, let him call to witness one just person, or two just persons, and let him not conceal nor hide; if its owner comes, he is most entitled to it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills."
"697","Chapter 71: The book of marriage. 729 - Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O company of youths, whoever of you is able to marry, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity; and whoever is not able, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"698","730 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us. And Abu Ja'far al-Mukharrami Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy."
"699","731 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: 'Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ibn al-Musayyib narrated to him, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who informed him, he said: 'Uthman ibn Maz'un wanted to live celibate, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him. Sa'd said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted that to him, we would have castrated ourselves."
"700","732 - 'Ali ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I proposed to a woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Did you look at her? He said: I said: No. He said: Then look at her, for it is more likely to bring affection between you."
"701","733 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah proposed to a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and look at her, for it is more lasting for what is between you."
"702","734 - 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah said. And Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and 'Ali said: He raises it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Do not practice najsh, and let no resident sell for a Bedouin, and let no man sell over the sale of his brother, and let no man propose over the proposal of his brother, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister. 'Ali added: So as to overturn what is in her vessel."
"703","735 - Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not fitting for a woman to stipulate the divorce of her sister so as to overturn her vessel."
"704","736 - Abu Zur'ah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: 'Abthar informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud in prayer, and the tashahhud in need; then he mentioned the tashahhud in prayer and the tashahhud in need, and said: And the tashahhud in need is that one says: Indeed all praise belongs to Allah; we praise Him, seek His help, and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls; whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He misguides, none can guide; and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recites three verses of the Qur'an: {Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims}. {And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you}. {O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word}."
"705","737 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, do you desire my sister? He said: What would I do? She said: You marry her. He said: Your sister? She said: Yes. He said: And do you love that? She said: I am not alone, and the one I most love to share good with me is my sister! He said: Then she is not lawful to me. She said: By Allah, I have been told that you are proposing to Durrah - or Dharrah, the doubt is from Zuhayr. He said: The daughter of Umm Salamah? She said: Yes. He said: By Allah, had she not been my stepdaughter under my care, she would not have been lawful to me; she is the daughter of my foster-brother; Thuwaybah nursed me and her father, so do not present your daughters or your sisters to me."
"706","738 - Rawh ibn al-Faraj, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Sabiq, narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara', from his father, he said: I met my uncle with a banner fastened, so I said: Where are you heading? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, to strike his neck and take his wealth."
"707","739 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Rifa'ah al-Qurazi, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that Rifa'ah ibn Samaw'al divorced his wife Tumaymah bint Wahb in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr married her, but was unable to consummate with her, so he divorced her without touching her; then Rifa'ah wanted to marry her - and he was her husband who had divorced her before 'Abd al-Rahman - so that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade him to marry her, saying: She is not lawful to you until she tastes the sweetness."
"708","740 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the wife of Rifa'ah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Rifa'ah divorced me with a divorce by which I became irrevocable from him, and I married 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, and he is with him like the fringe of a garment. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Do you want to return to Rifa'ah? No, until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness."
"709","741 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us. And Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla informed us, from 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far - that is al-Mukharrimi - from 'Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the muhallil and the one for whom it is done."
"710","742 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Dawud - meaning Ibn Abi Hind - informed us, he said: 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt, and the paternal aunt over her brother's daughter, or a woman over her maternal aunt, or the maternal aunt over her sister's daughter; the younger is not married over the elder, nor the elder over the younger."
"711","743 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who marries without the permission of his master and his family is a fornicator."
"712","744 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fosterage makes unlawful what birth makes unlawful."
"713","745 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us that 'Amrah, the daughter of 'Abd al-Rahman, informed him that she heard 'A'ishah saying: There was revealed in the Qur'an ten known sucklings, meaning what makes unlawful from fosterage. 'Amrah said: Then 'A'ishah mentioned and said: Afterwards five were revealed."
"714","746 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Wuhayb, from Ayyub, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One or two sucks do not make unlawful."
"715","747 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: The nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn 'Amr came - and she was under Abu Hudhayfah ibn 'Utbah - and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon us while I am in light dress, and we used to consider him a son; and Abu Hudhayfah had adopted him just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adopted Zayd, then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then ordered her to nurse Salim, so she nursed him five sucklings, and he became like her son by fosterage. For that reason 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to order her brothers and the daughters of her brothers to nurse whomsoever 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, loved to see her and enter upon her, even if grown, five sucklings, then he would enter upon her; while Umm Salamah and the rest of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused that anyone enter upon them by that nursing, until he is nursed in the cradle, and they said to 'A'ishah: By Allah, we do not know; perhaps it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Salim apart from people."
"716","748 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from al-Ash'ath, from his father, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while a man was with her, and said: Who is this? She said: My brother by fosterage. He said: Look to who your brothers are, for fosterage is only from hunger."
"717","749 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah. 750 - And Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her - one of them adding to the other - she said: My uncle came after the veil was imposed, asking permission to enter upon me, but I did not permit him; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, so I asked him, and he said: Permit him, for he is your uncle. I said: Only the woman nursed me, and the man did not nurse me? He said: May your right hand be dusted, permit him, for he is your uncle."
"718","751 - 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both. And 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The daughter of Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is the daughter of my brother by fosterage."
"719","752 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Nubayh ibn Wahb, the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Dar, that 'Umar ibn 'Abdillah wanted to marry Talhah ibn 'Umar to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr while both were in ihram, so he sent to Aban ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Affan to attend that. He said: So Aban disapproved of that to him, while he was the leader of the pilgrimage, and Aban said: I heard 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram does not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"720","753 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, the nephew of Maymunah, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif while we were both lawful."
"721","754 - Ibn al-Muqri and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Abu al-Sha'tha', that Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"722","754/2 - So I informed al-Zuhri of it, and he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm informed me - and she is his maternal aunt - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while he was lawful, and she was lawful."
"723","755 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan and 'Abdillah, the two sons of Muhammad - he said: And al-Hasan was the more reliable of them - from their father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage, and the meat of domestic donkeys at the time of Khaybar. And Sufyan used to say: al-Hasan was the better of them."
"724","756 - Ibn al-Muqri said: And Sufyan narrated it to us with it another time and mentioned it, and said: From their father, he heard 'Ali saying to Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage, and the meat of domestic donkeys."
"725","757 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah al-Juhani, from his father: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage."
"726","758 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to us, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we completed our 'umrah, he said to us: Enjoy yourselves with these women - and enjoyment with us that day was marriage. He said: So we presented that to the women, but they refused unless we fixed a term between us and them. He said: So we mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do so. He said: So I and a cousin of mine went out, with me a cloak and with him a cloak, and his cloak was better than mine, and I was younger than him. He said: So we came to a woman and presented that to her, and my youth pleased her, while my cousin's cloak pleased her, so she said: A cloak like a cloak. So I married her, and the term between me and her was ten days. He said: So I spent that night with her, then I went in the morning to the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing, delivering a sermon between the Hijr and the Door, saying: O people, I had permitted you enjoyment with these women; but Allah has forbidden that until the Day of Resurrection, so whoever has any of them with him, let him release her, and do not take anything of what you gave them."
"727","759 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void; if he enters with her, she has the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"728","760 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"729","761 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"730","762 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"731","763 - Abu Bakr Hamdan ibn Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn al-Sindi and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Jawhari narrated to us, they said: Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. 764 - And Sharik also joined it and attributed it."
"732","765 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated it to me, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, Juwayriyah bint al-Harith fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, or a cousin of his. He said: So she contracted kitabah for herself, and she was a sweet, charming woman; hardly anyone saw her without being captivated by her. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help for her kitabah. She said: By Allah, it was only that I saw her at the door of the chamber and disliked her, and I knew he would see in her what I saw. So she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyah the daughter of al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the chief of his people, and there has befallen me of the affair what is not hidden from you, so I fell in the share of Thabit, or a cousin of his, and I contracted kitabah for myself, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help for my kitabah. He said: Do you have something better than that? She said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I pay your kitabah and marry you? She said: Yes. He said: I have done so. And the news went out among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, so the people said: The in-laws of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so they released what was in their hands of the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq. His marrying her freed one hundred households of Banu al-Mustaliq; we know no woman who was a greater blessing upon her people than her."
"733","766 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Ibn Abi Salamah, he said: Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I heard something from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which is more pleasing to me than such-and-such: No one is afflicted with a calamity, and he mentioned part of the hadith. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her and proposed to her, so she said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In me are three traits which I fear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a woman of intense jealousy, I am a woman none of my guardians is present to marry me, and I am a woman with children. So 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, heard of that and became angry for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more intensely than he became angry for himself when she said to him: O son of al-Khattab, in me is such-and-such. So what she said reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to her and said: As for what you mentioned of your jealousy, I shall supplicate Allah, exalted, to remove it from you; and as for what you mentioned of your children, Allah will suffice them; and as for what you mentioned that there is here none of your guardians to marry you, there is none of your guardians, present or absent, who dislikes me. So she said to her son: Marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he married her to him."
"734","767 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us and said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously-married woman is not married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not married until she is asked permission. It was said: And what is her permission, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That she remains silent. The hadith is al-Darimi's."
"735","768 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Mukharrami and 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating, from Dhakwan Abu 'Amr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, he said: Seek permission. And al-Mukharrami said: Consult women regarding their private parts. It was said: But the virgin is shy and remains silent? He said: Then her silence is her permission. And al-Mukharrami said: She is shy. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it is her permission."
"736","769 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from 'Abdillah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously-married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and a virgin is consulted regarding herself, and her silence is her consent."
"737","770 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And in what I read to Ibn Nafi', from Malik, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi', the two sons of Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, from Khansa' bint Khidham al-Ansariyyah, may Allah be pleased with them both: That her father married her off while she was previously married, and she disliked that, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he annulled her marriage."
"738","771 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: 'Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and consummated with me when I was nine years old."
"739","772 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, from Sulayman - meaning Ibn Bilal - from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Habib, that he heard 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah saying: Yusuf ibn Mahak informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, their seriousness is seriousness and their jest is seriousness: marriage, divorce, and return."
"740","773 - Yahya ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while she was in the land of Abyssinia; al-Najashi married her to him and gave her a dowry of four thousand, and prepared her from his own, and sent her with Shurahbil ibn Hasanah; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not send anything to her. And the dowry of his wives was four hundred dirhams."
"741","774 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, with this chain, similar to it."
"742","775 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us that he heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, married a woman of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How much did you give her as dowry? He said: A date-stone of gold. Ibn Abi Najih said: The nawah is five dirhams, the nashsh is twenty dirhams, and the uqiyyah is forty dirhams."
"743","776 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: While we were among the people, a woman said: I have given myself to you, O Messenger of Allah! Give your opinion about me! So a man stood and said: Marry her to me! He said: Go and seek, even an iron ring. He said: So he went and did not bring anything, not even an iron ring. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have anything of the chapters of the Qur'an with you? He said: Yes. He said: So he married her to him for what he had of the chapters of the Qur'an."
"744","777 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Bishr - meaning Ibn al-Sari - narrated to us, from Dawud - meaning Ibn Qays - from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Our dowry when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us was ten uqiyyahs."
"745","778 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - informed us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdillah. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us - and the hadith is his - he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdillah, regarding a man who married a woman and did not stipulate for her nor touch her until he died. He said: So he turned them away, then said: I say about it by my opinion; if it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is wrong, it is from me: I see for her the dowry of a woman of her women, neither deficient nor excessive, and upon her is the waiting period, and for her is inheritance. He said: So Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Barwa' bint Washiq - a woman of Banu Ruwas - and Banu Ruwas is a clan of Banu 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah."
"746","779 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"747","780 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And in what I read to Ibn Nafi', from Malik ibn Anas, from Nafi', from 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. And shighar is that a man marries a man his daughter on condition that the other marries him his daughter, with no dowry between them."
"748","781 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - he said: Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"749","782 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man has two wives and inclines to one of them, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen."
"750","783 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, and 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud informed me of the hadith of 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet, said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out with her."
"751","784 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Sunnah is that when one marries a virgin, he stays with her seven days, and when he marries a previously-married woman, he stays with her three days."
"752","785 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, he would go out with her with him. And he used to allot to each of his women her day and her night, except that Sawdah bint Zam'ah gave her day and her night to 'A'ishah, seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"753","786 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf married, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"754","787 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Hafsah, or one of his wives, and held a wedding feast for her of dates and sawiq."
"755","788 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Usamah ibn al-Hadi, from 'Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth; do not come to women in their backs."
"756","789 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who comes to a man or a woman in the back passage."
"757","790 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: 'Abd ibn Zam'ah and Sa'd disputed about the son of the slave-woman of Zam'ah. Sa'd said: My brother advised me, when I come to Mecca, to take the son of the slave-woman of Zam'ah, for he is my son. So 'Abd ibn Zam'ah said: The son of my father's slave-woman, born on my father's bed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a clear resemblance to 'Utbah, and said: He is yours, O 'Abd ibn Zam'ah; and the child belongs to the bed; and veil yourself from him, O Sawdah."
"758","791 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdillah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Marzuq al-Tujibi, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ruwayfi' ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day - or whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not water his water the child of another."
"759","792 - Muhammad ibn 'Awf narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of donkeys, and every beast of prey with fangs, and that captive women be approached until they give birth."
"760","Chapter 72: The book of divorce. 793 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman, the freedman of 'Urwah, asking Ibn 'Umar - while Abu al-Zubayr listened - and said: What do you think about a man who divorces his wife while menstruating? He said: 'Abdillah divorced his wife while menstruating in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so 'Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him take her back. So he returned her to me, and said: When she is pure, let him divorce or keep. Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period}, at the beginning of their waiting period."
"761","794 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: 'Uqbah narrated to me, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I divorced my wife."
"762","794 (m) - And al-Za'farani narrated to us - and the hadith is his - he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I divorced my wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating, so 'Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Order him to take her back until she is pure, then she menstruates another menstruation; when she is pure, let him divorce her if he wishes before he touches her, or keep her; for that is the waiting period which Allah ordered that women be divorced for."
"763","795 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so 'Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order him to take her back until she is pure. So I said to Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: Was that divorce counted? He said: What then!"
"764","796 - Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, they said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, from Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he divorced his wife during menstruation - and al-Za'farani said: while she was menstruating - so 'Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order him to take her back, then divorce her while she is pure or pregnant. Yusuf said: So 'Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"765","797 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Nafi', from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed him that 'Uwaymir al-'Ajlani - then he mentioned in the story of li'an - he said: So he divorced her thrice before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him. Ibn Shihab said: So that was the sunnah of the two who invoke curses."
"766","798 - Muhammad ibn 'Awf ibn Sufyan al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Duhaym narrated to us, he said: al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri: Which of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge from him? He said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the daughter of al-Jawn, when she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drew near her, said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have sought refuge in a Mighty One; join your family. al-Zuhri said: Join your family is a divorce."
"767","799 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ordered to give his wives the choice, he began with me and said: I inform you of news, and it is no harm upon you not to hasten until you consult your parents. Then he said: Indeed Allah said: {O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world} - until he reached - {then indeed Allah has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward}. So I said: In which of this do I consult my parents? Indeed I desire Allah and His Messenger and the abode of the Hereafter. She said: Then the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did the like of what I did."
"768","800 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice; was it a divorce?"
"769","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ismail - meaning Ibn Ulayyah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said concerning the husband of Barirah: That was Mughith, a slave of Banu so-and-so; by Allah, I can see him now following her in the streets of Madinah, weeping."
"770","Muhammad ibn Abdillah Abu Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham - he is al-Mughirah ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi - narrated to us, from Wuhayb, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): the husband of Barirah was a slave."
"771","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce concerning what one does not own, nor any emancipation concerning what one does not own."
"772","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Salamah ibn Sakhr al-Ansari, he said: I was a man who had been given of desire for women what no one else had been given. When Ramadan came, I made zihar from my wife until it ended, fearing that I would approach her at night and then continue, until morning overtook me while I was unable to stop. While she was serving me one night, something of her was uncovered to me, so I fell upon her. In the morning I went to my people and told them my story, and said to them: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of my matter. They said: No, by Allah, we will not do it; we fear that Quran will be revealed concerning us, or that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will say something about us whose disgrace will remain upon us. Rather, go and do as you see fit. So I went until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him my story. He said to me: Are you the one? I said: I am the one. He said: Are you the one? I said: I am the one. He said: Are you the one? I said: I am the one, so carry out the ruling of Allah concerning me, for I am patient and hopeful of reward. He said: Free a slave. He said: So I struck the side of my neck and said: By the One who sent you with the truth, O Messenger of Allah, I own nothing besides it this morning. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did what befell me befall me except because of fasting? He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we spent our night destitute with no supper. He said: Go to the keeper of the charity of Banu Zurayq, and tell him to hand it over to you; feed on your behalf from it a wasq of dates to sixty poor persons, then seek help with the rest for yourself and your family. He said: So I returned to my people and said: I found with you hardship and bad counsel, and I found with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ease and blessing; he has ordered for me your charity, so hand it over to me. He said: So they handed it over to me."
"773","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a man of Banu Zurayq called Salamah ibn Sakhr: then he mentioned the hadith similarly in abridged form, and said at its end: He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates, and he gave them to me, close to fifteen sa, and said: Give this in charity. He said: O Messenger of Allah, upon one poorer than me and my family? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat it, you and your family."
"774","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mamar ibn Abdillah ibn Hanzalah, from Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam, he said: Khuwaylah bint Thalabah narrated to me - and she was with Aws ibn Samit, the brother of Ubadah ibn al-Samit - she said: He came to me one day and spoke to me about something while annoyed, so I answered him back, and he became angry and said: You are to me as the back of my mother. Then he went out and sat in the gathering place of his people, then he returned and wanted me, so I refused him, and he wrestled me and I wrestled him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. So I said: No, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you shall not reach her until Allah judges concerning me and you. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of what I met from him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is your husband and your cousin, so fear Allah and keep good company with him. She said: I had not left before the Quran came down: Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband, until it reached the expiation. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command him to free a slave. I said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, he has no slave to free. He said: Command him to fast two consecutive months. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man with no ability to fast. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor persons. I said: O Prophet of Allah, he has nothing with which to feed. He said: We shall help him with a basket of dates - and the basket is a container holding thirty sa. I said: And I shall help him with another basket. He said: You have done well; let him give it in charity."
"775","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Ammar narrated to me, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after having made zihar from his wife and then having intercourse with her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I made zihar from my wife and then I fell upon her before expiating. He said: What carried you to that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: Do not approach her until you do what Allah the Exalted has commanded."
"776","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any harm, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."
"777","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And from what I read to Abdillah ibn Nafi, and Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, that she informed him from Habibah bint Sahl al-Ansariyyah, that she was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the dawn prayer and found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this? She said: I am Habibah bint Sahl. He said: What is your matter? She said: Neither I nor Thabit ibn Qays - meaning her husband. When Thabit came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: This is Habibah bint Sahl, and she has mentioned what Allah willed that she mention. So Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, all that he gave me is with me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Thabit: Take from her. So he took from her, and she remained among her family."
"778","Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, he said: Qurad Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), she said: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: I blame nothing of Thabit in religion or character, but I fear disbelief in Islam. So he said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to return to him his garden, and he separated between them."
"779","Abu Muhammad said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman also narrated it, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), except that he did not mention at its end: and he separated between them. Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated it to us, from his father, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"780","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best charity is what is given out of sufficiency, and begin with those you support. Abu Hurayrah said: Your wife says: Spend on me or divorce me; and your child says: Spend on me, to whom do you leave me? And your servant says: Spend on me or sell me."
"781","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I was asked about the two who invoke curses whether they are separated, during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr, and I did not know what to say. So I stood from my place to the house of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, are the two who invoke curses separated? He said: Glory be to Allah, yes. The first who asked about that was so-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man among us who sees his wife in indecency? If he speaks, he speaks of a grave matter, and if he is silent, he is silent over the like of that! He said: So he did not answer him. He said: When the next day came he came to him and said: That which I asked about, I have been afflicted with it. So Allah sent down this verse in Surat al-Nur: And those who accuse their wives, until it reached: and the fifth, that the anger of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. So he began with the man, admonishing him and reminding him, and informing him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. So he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not lied. Then he turned to the woman, admonishing her and reminding her, and informing her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. So she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, he is indeed a liar. He said: So he began with the man, and he testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is of the liars. Then he turned to the woman, and she testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the liars, and the fifth that the anger of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. Then he separated between them."
"782","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between the two who invoke curses, and said: Your account is upon Allah; one of you is lying; there is no way for you to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth? He said: You have no wealth from her; if you were truthful to her, then it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied, then that is further from it for you."
"783","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man invoked curses against his wife and disowned her child, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them, and attached the child to the woman."
"784","al-Rabi ibn Sulayman informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me, from his father, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked curses between al-Ajlani and his wife, and she was pregnant."
"785","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad, that Uwaymir came to Asim ibn Adi and mentioned part of the hadith. He said: So he invoked curses against her, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you keep her, you have wronged her. He said: So he divorced her, and it became afterwards a practice for those who invoked curses after them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch; if she brings him dark, intensely black-eyed, large-buttocked, thick-legged, then I do not think Uwaymir but that he told the truth; and if she brings him reddish as though a small gecko, then I do not think Uwaymir but that he lied. He said: So she brought him according to the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described, confirming Uwaymir. He said: And he was afterwards attributed to his mother."
"786","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). He said: And Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then she married. So her husband came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had accepted Islam along with her, and she knew of my Islam. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"787","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ghasil - narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from Abu Usayd, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we set out to a garden called al-Shawt, until we reached two gardens. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit here. Then he entered, and al-Jawniyyah had been brought and lodged in the palm-house: Umaymah bint al-Numan ibn Sharahil, with a nurse caring for her. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, he said: Give yourself to me. She said: Does a queen give herself to a commoner? He said: So he reached out his hand to place it upon her to calm her, and she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: You have sought refuge in a place of refuge. Then he came out to us and said: O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two razqiyyah garments and take her to her family."
"788","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Hammad Masadah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ishaq, from his aunt Zaynab bint Kab, from al-Furayiah bint Malik, that her husband went out seeking slaves of his, and overtook them at al-Qadum, and they attacked him and killed him. And she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and mentioned that she was in a house far from her family, and that she wanted to move to them, so he permitted her. She said: So I went out until, when I was in the chambers - or she said: I had passed the chambers - he called me - or she said: he sent to me - and called me, and said to me: Remain in the house of your husband in which the news of him came to you, until the decree reaches its term. She said: When it was the time of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), he sent to me and asked me, and I informed him."
"789","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdillah al-Uwaysi informed us, from Malik, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, that Abu Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably while absent, and sent to her his agent with barley, and she disliked it. So he said: By Allah, you have nothing upon us. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. So he said: You have no maintenance upon him. And he ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik, then he said: That is a woman whom my companions visit; so observe your waiting period with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man - you may lay aside your garments - and when you become lawful, inform me. She said: When I became lawful, I mentioned to him that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Abu Jahm, he never puts his stick down from his shoulder; and as for Muawiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth; marry Usamah ibn Zayd. She said: So I disliked it. Then he said: Marry Usamah ibn Zayd. So I married him, and Allah put good in him, and I was happy with him."
"790","Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm ibn Sukhayr al-Adawi, he said: I heard Fatimah bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) say: Her husband divorced her three times, and the Messenger of Allah assigned for her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"791","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - informed us that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him, that Abu Salamah informed him, that he and Ibn Abbas gathered with Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him). They mentioned the man who dies leaving a wife, and she gives birth nights afterwards. So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Her release is the later of the two terms. And Abu Salamah said: When she delivers, she becomes lawful. So they disputed between them over that. So Abu Hurayrah said: I am with my nephew - meaning Abu Salamah. So they sent Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salamah, and he asked her. So Umm Salamah mentioned that Subayiah bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah - her husband died, and she gave birth nights after him - and that a man of Banu Abd al-Dar, called Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, proposed to her and informed her that she had become lawful, and she wanted to marry another. So Abu al-Sanabil said to her: You have not become lawful. So Subayiah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered her to marry."
"792","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh, that she sought khul in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her - or she was ordered - to observe a waiting period of one menstruation."
"793","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Said al-Attar and Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three nights. And al-Attar said: Sufyan informed us."
"794","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her): a relative or kinsman of hers died, so she called for yellow dye and wiped her forearms, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - or the Messenger of Allah said - (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three, except over a husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten days."
"795","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Hisham, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. [TEXT BREAKS OFF HERE - FLAG: matn appears truncated in source]"
"796","And Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Said al-Attar narrated to us - and this is his hadith - he said: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three, except over a husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten days. She shall not apply kohl, nor wear a dyed garment except a garment of asb, nor touch perfume except at the end of her purity."
"797","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, they said: Yahya - he is Ibn Abi Bukayr - narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, he said: Budayl narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet: A woman whose husband has died shall not wear saffron-dyed garments, nor mumashshaqah, nor jewelry, nor dye with henna, nor apply kohl."
"798","He said: And Budayl narrated to me, that al-Hasan ibn Muslim said: I did not see them regard aloeswood as harmful."
"799","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from her mother, that a woman whose husband had died complained of her eye. So they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned kohl, and said: We fear for her eye. He said: One of you used to remain in her house in her worst clothes for a year; when a dog passed, she threw a dung. So no; four months and ten days."
"800","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said, from Matar, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Do not confuse against us the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the waiting period of the umm walad is the waiting period of the one whose husband died."
"801","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, he said: Abu Rimthah al-Taymi informed me, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of mine. He said: Your son? I said: I testify to it. He said: He shall not bear your offense, nor shall you bear his. He said: And I saw the red dye of gray hair."
"802","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslims, their blood is equal; the lowest of them strives to grant protection; and they are one hand against others."
"803","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Salih informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: There were Qurayzah and al-Nadir, and al-Nadir was nobler than Qurayzah. When a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah, blood money of one hundred wasqs of dates was paid; and when a man of Qurayzah killed a man of Banu al-Nadir, he was killed for him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah, and they said: Hand him to us that we may kill him. So they said: Between us and you is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they came to him, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down: And if you judge, judge between them with justice. He said: So justice is a soul for a soul. Then was revealed: Do they seek the judgment of ignorance?"
"804","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, from Uqbah ibn Aws, from Abdillah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily every boast of the pre-Islamic age, counted or claimed, of blood or wealth, is under my feet, except what was of the watering of pilgrims and the custodianship of the House. Then he said: Verily the blood money of accidental killing, what is by whip or stick: one hundred camels, of them forty in whose bellies are their young."
"805","Ibrahim ibn Abdillah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja al-Sulami, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuzai, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is afflicted with blood or a wound - and khabl is a wound - he has the choice among one of three; if he wants a fourth, then restrain his hand: between retaliating, or pardoning, or taking the blood money. If he takes something of that, then transgresses afterwards, then for him is the Fire, abiding therein forever."
"806","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed us, he said: I heard Mujahid, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: Retaliation was among the Children of Israel, and there was no blood money among them. So Allah said to this nation: O you who believe, retaliation is prescribed for you in murder: the free for the free, the slave for the slave, the female for the female; then whoever is pardoned anything by his brother. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: So pardon is to accept blood money in intentional killing: then following with kindness and payment to him with excellence. He said: Upon this one is to follow with kindness, and upon this one is to pay with excellence: That is a lightening from your Lord, from what was prescribed upon those before you: then whoever transgresses after that, for him is a painful punishment."
"807","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Two women of Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other, killing her and what was in her womb. So they disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the blood money of her fetus is a ghurrah, a slave or slave-girl, and judged the blood money of the woman upon her kin, and her child and those with them inherited her. Hamal ibn al-Nabighah al-Hudhali said: O Messenger of Allah, how should I pay for one who neither drank nor ate, nor spoke nor cried? The like of that is void. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is only of the brethren of soothsayers, because of his rhymed speech."
"808","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Qusayt, from Ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition, and in that expedition were Abu Qatadah al-Ansari and Muhallim ibn Jaththamah ibn Qays, and I was among them. While we were thus, Amir ibn al-Adbat al-Ashjai passed by us and greeted us with the greeting of Islam. So we held back from him, then Muhallim ibn Jaththamah attacked him and killed him, and took a camel of his and a water-skin of milk that was with him. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Quran came down concerning us: O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, verify, to the end of the verse."
"809","al-Muharibi said: Ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: I heard Ziyad ibn Damrah ibn Sad al-Sulami narrate to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: My father and grandfather narrated to me - and they had witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, then sat in the shade of a tree. Then al-Aqra ibn Habis and Uyaynah ibn Badr came to him; Uyaynah seeking the blood of al-Ashjai, and al-Aqra defending him. They disputed long before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather will you accept blood money, fifty in our journey and fifty when we return? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept with them until they accepted the blood money. When they accepted the blood money, they said: Where is your companion, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) may seek forgiveness for him? So a tall man stood, wearing a suit, prepared therein for execution, until he sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your name? He said: I am Muhallim ibn Jaththamah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim ibn Jaththamah! So he stood from before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wiping his tears with the edge of his cloak."
"810","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nadlah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah: two women who were co-wives; one of them threw at the other a stone or a tent-pole, and she miscarried a fetus. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning it a ghurrah, a slave or slave-girl, and placed it upon the kin of the woman."
"811","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Khalid al-Tabari narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every clan is its blood-money liability."
"812","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood money of the fingers of the hands and feet is equal; for every finger, ten camels."
"813","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the fingers, ten each."
"814","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This and this are equal - and he joined his thumb and little finger - meaning in blood money."
"815","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This and this are equal, and this and this are equal: the little finger and the thumb, and the molar and the front tooth."
"816","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for them a letter, in it: And the leg is fifty, and the hand is fifty; and for the fingers of the hands and feet, for every finger of them, ten camels; and for the nose, when completely cut off, one hundred camels; and for the tooth, five camels."
"817","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said: Abbad - meaning Ibn al-Awwam - narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the fingers, ten each; and for wounds exposing the bone, five each."
"818","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for a wound exposing the bone five camels, and for a wound reaching the brain a third of the blood money."
"819","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, he said: Malik informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that Sad ibn Ubadah said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think, if I find a man with my wife, should I give him respite until I bring four witnesses? He said: Yes."
"820","Muhammad ibn Muslim Warah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mansur - meaning Ibn al-Mutamir - from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man of Banu Mudlij had a slave-girl from whom he had a son, and he used her for service. When the boy grew, he called her one day and said: Do such-and-such. So the boy said: She will not come to you; until when will you command my mother? He said: So his father became angry and threw his sword at him, striking his leg or other part and severing it. So the boy bled and died. So he went with a group of his people to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: O enemy of yourself, are you the one who killed your son? Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A father is not retaliated against for his son, I would have killed you. Bring his blood money. He said: So he brought him one hundred and twenty or thirty camels. He said: So he selected from them one hundred and gave them to his heirs, leaving his father."
"821","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sad, that a man peeped through a hole into the chamber of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. So he said: Had I known you were looking, I would have thrust it into your eye; seeking permission was only made because of looking."
"822","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever peeps into the house of people without their permission, and they gouge his eye, then there is neither blood money for him nor retaliation."
"823","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man peeps at you in your house, and you throw a pebble at him and gouge his eye, there is no sin upon you."
"824","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ata informing, he said: Safwan ibn Yala informed me, from Yala ibn Umayyah, he said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of hardship."
"825","And Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us - and the hadith is his - he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah narrated to him, from Yala ibn Umayyah, he said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of hardship, and it was my most cherished deed in my soul. I had a hireling, and he fought a man; one of them bit the other, who pulled his finger, and his front tooth fell out. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who voided his tooth. Ata said: And I think Safwan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he leave his hand in your mouth for you to bite it as a stallion bites?"
"826","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest, he stood among us as a preacher. Abu Muhammad said: I have written it in the Siyar."
"827","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I said to Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides the Quran? He said: No, by the One who splits the grain and creates the soul, except that Allah grants a servant understanding in His Book, and what is in this sheet. He said: I said: And what is in this sheet? He said: Blood money, freeing the captive, and that no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever."
"828","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: The first time I saw al-Zuhri, I asked him about this hadith, and he narrated to me, he said: Said and Abu Salamah narrated to me that they heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The senseless animal, its wound is void; the mine is void; the well is void; and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"829","Ibn al-Muqri said: And he narrated it to us another time, and did not say in it: And the well is void."
"830","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Haram ibn Sad: a she-camel of al-Bara entered a garden of people and spoiled it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the guarding of property is upon its owners by day, and upon the owners of livestock what they damage by night. Ibn al-Muqri said: And perhaps he said: Upon the owners of livestock what their livestock spoil by night. And he said once: What their livestock damage by night."
"831","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me, from a man of the companions of the Prophet of the Ansar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affirmed qasamah as it was in the pre-Islamic age."
"832","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: Abdullah ibn Sahl was found slain - and once he said: dead - in a well of the wells of Khaybar, or a spring of its springs. So his uncles and his brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl - who had witnessed Badr - came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). His brother Abd al-Rahman spoke, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The elder, the elder. So his uncle Muhayyisah spoke and said: O Messenger of Allah, we found Abdullah slain in a well of the wells of Khaybar. He said: Then fifty of you shall swear that the Jews killed him. They said: How can we swear over what we did not see? He said: Then the Jews will clear you with fifty. They said: How can we accept them while they are polytheists? And Ibn al-Muqri said: And he said another time: The Jews will clear you with fifty, swearing that they did not kill him and know no killer. So they said: How can we accept the oaths of polytheist people? He said: Then fifty of you shall swear that they killed him. They said: How can we swear when we did not see? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from himself, and a young she-camel of it kicked me."
"833","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas say: Abu Layla ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that he informed him, from men of the elders of his people, that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah went out to Khaybar because of hardship that befell them. Then Muhayyisah was told that Abdullah ibn Sahl had been killed and thrown in a spring or well. So he came to the Jews and said: By Allah, you killed him. They said: By Allah, we did not kill him. Then he returned until he came to his people and mentioned that to them. Then he, his brother Huwayyisah - who was older - and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came; Muhayyisah went to speak, he being the one who was at Khaybar. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muhayyisah: Honor the elder, honor the elder - meaning age - so Huwayyisah spoke, then Muhayyisah spoke. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Either they pay the blood money of your companion, or they announce war. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to them concerning that, and they wrote: By Allah, we did not kill him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Huwayyisah, Muhayyisah, and Abd al-Rahman: Swear, and you shall establish the blood of your companion. They said: No. He said: Then the Jews shall swear for you. They said: They are not Muslims. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from himself; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to them one hundred she-camels, until they were brought into their house. Sahl said: A red she-camel of them kicked me."
"834","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah and Rafi ibn Khadij, that they narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah ibn Masud came to Khaybar for a need, and parted in its palms. So Abdullah ibn Sahl was killed. Then his brother - Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl - and his cousins - Muhayyisah and Huwayyisah, sons of Masud - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abd al-Rahman began to speak, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor the elder - meaning: the eldest begins speaking - and Abd al-Rahman was younger than his two companions. So they spoke concerning the killing of their companion. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish your slain and your companion by the oaths of fifty of you. So they said: We did not witness; how can we swear? So he said: The Jews will clear you by the oaths of fifty of them. So they said: Disbelieving people. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money. Sahl said: I caught a she-camel of those camels that kicked me a kick from their resting place."
"835","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Abi al-Azhar narrated to us in Baghdad, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Isa ibn Yazid, he said: Jarir ibn Yazid narrated to me that he heard Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, that he heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prescribed penalty carried out in the land is better for its people than being rained upon for thirty mornings."
"836","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him in this world and the Hereafter."
"837","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering, and he said: Pledge to me that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery - he recited the verse to them - so whoever of you fulfills, his reward is upon Allah; and whoever commits something of that and is punished for it, it is an expiation for him; and whoever commits something of that and Allah covers him, then he is to Allah: if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"838","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: A Makhzumiyyah woman used to borrow goods and deny them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her hand cut. So her family came to Usamah and spoke to him, and Usamah spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Usamah, do I see you interceding concerning a prescribed penalty of Allah? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher and said: Those before you were destroyed only because when the noble among them stole they left him, and when the weak among them stole they cut him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, had it been Fatimah bint Muhammad, I would have cut her hand. He said: So he cut the hand of the Makhzumiyyah."
"839","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Layth, from his father, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her): Quraysh were concerned by the affair of the Makhzumiyyah who stole. So they said: Who will speak concerning her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he mentioned the hadith."
"840","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Layth - meaning Ibn Sad - narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Quraysh were concerned by the affair of the woman who stole."
"841","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given choice between two matters but he chose the easier of them; nor did he retaliate from a man for a wrong except for something of the limits of Allah, which is not left for anyone."
"842","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the child until he grows, and from the insane until he regains reason."
"843","Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) examined me on the day of Uhud for fighting while I was fourteen, and did not permit me; and when it was the day of the Trench, he examined me while I was fifteen, and permitted me. He said: So I came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) - and Umar was then caliph - and informed him of this hadith. So he said: This is indeed a boundary between the minor and the major. So he wrote to his governors: Assign for one of fifteen, and whoever is below that, join him to the dependents."
"844","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me, take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the previously married, one hundred lashes then stoning; and the virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year."
"845","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, Zayd ibn Khalid, and Shibl, they said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man came and said: I adjure you by Allah, judge between us only by the Book of Allah. Then his opponent stood - and he was more understanding than him - and said: He spoke the truth; judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me. He said: Speak. He said: My son was a laborer for this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. So I was told that upon my son is stoning, so I ransomed from him with one hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked men of knowledge, and they informed me that upon my son is one hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that upon the wife of this one is stoning. So he said: I shall judge between you two by the Book of Allah: the hundred sheep and the servant are returned; and upon your son is one hundred lashes and exile for a year; and go, O Unays, to the wife of this one - if she confesses, stone her. So she confessed, and he stoned her."
"846","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I feared that time would pass over people until one would say: We do not find stoning in the Book of Allah, and they would go astray by leaving an obligation Allah sent down. Verily stoning is true upon whoever commits adultery when married, when proof is established, or pregnancy, or confession. Verily the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned with him."
"847","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdillah (may Allah be pleased with them both): a man of Aslam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed to adultery before him; then he confessed and he turned away from him; then he confessed and he turned away from him, until he testified against himself four times. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you mad? He said: No. He said: Are you married? He said: Yes. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was stoned at the prayer place. When the stones pained him, he fled. So he was caught and stoned until he died. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good of him, and did not pray over him."
"848","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Samit, nephew of Abu Hurayrah, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: al-Aslami came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and testified against himself that he had approached a woman unlawfully four times, each time he turned away from him. Then he faced him the fifth time and said: Did you penetrate her? He said: Yes. He said: Until that of you disappeared in that of her, as the applicator disappears in the kohl container and the rope in the well? He said: Yes; I approached from her unlawfully what a man approaches from his wife lawfully. He said: What do you want by this statement? He said: I want you to purify me. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was stoned. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men of his companions, one saying to his fellow: Look at this one whom Allah covered, but his soul did not leave him until he was stoned like a dog. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent to them. Then he traveled a while until he passed by the carcass of a donkey with its leg raised. So he said: Where are so-and-so and so-and-so? They said: We are these two, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Dismount and eat from the carcass of this donkey. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah forgive you, who would eat from this? He said: What you just took from the honor of your brother is worse than eating carrion. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is now in the rivers of Paradise, plunging therein."
"849","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him): a woman of Juhaynah confessed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to adultery. She said: I am pregnant. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and said: Treat her well; when she delivers, inform me. So he did. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her, and her clothes were tied over her, then he ordered her stoning and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you stoned her then pray over her? So he said: She has repented a repentance that, had it been divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, would have encompassed them. Did you find better than that she gave herself to Allah?"
"850","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed us and said: O people, establish the prescribed penalties upon your slaves, those married of them and those unmarried. A slave-girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery, so he ordered me to flog her. So I came to her, and she was newly delivered of childbirth. So I feared that if I flogged her she would die - or he said: I would kill her - so I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. So he said: You did well."
"851","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed me that one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the Ansar informed him: a man of them complained until he wasted away, his skin upon his bone. Then a slave-girl of one of them entered, and he inclined to her and fell upon her. When men of his people entered upon him visiting him, he informed them of that and said: Seek a ruling for me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fell upon a slave-girl who entered upon me. So they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen anyone among people in distress like his; were we to carry him to you, his bones would fall apart; he is but skin upon bone. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them a hundred stalks, and they struck him one strike."
"852","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Jurayj narrate from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man committed adultery, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he was flogged the penalty; then he was informed that he had been married, so he ordered him and he was stoned. Abu Muhammad said: Uthman ibn Umar, Abu Asim, and others narrated it, saying: A man committed adultery and was flogged, and they did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"853","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Maiz al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery. So he turned away from him, until he said that four times. So he said: Take him and stone him. So they went, and when he was stoned and felt the stones, he fled running. Then he passed a man with a camel's jawbone, who struck him and killed him. So they mentioned his flight to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he felt the stones. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not leave him?"
"854","al-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"855","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the slave-girl when she commits adultery and is unmarried. So he said: If she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, sell her even for a rope. Ibn Shihab said: I do not know whether after the third or the fourth; and the rope is a cord."
"856","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jew and a Jewess."
"857","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Asbat - meaning Ibn Nasr - narrated to us, from Simak, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from his father Wail ibn Hujr, that a woman was fallen upon by a man in the darkness of dawn while she was heading to the mosque unwillingly, struggling against herself. So she sought help from a man who passed by her, and her assailant fled. Then a group of people passed by her, so she sought help from them, and they caught the one she had sought help from, while the other outran them and went. So they brought him leading him to her, and he said: I am only the one who helped you, and the other has gone. So they brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she informed him that he had fallen upon her, and the people informed him that they caught him running. So he said: I was helping her against her assailant, but these caught me and seized me. So she said: He lied; he is the one who fell upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him and stone him. He said: Then a man stood and said: Do not stone him, stone me; I am the one who did the deed to her - and he confessed. So three gathered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the one who fell upon her, the one who helped her, and the woman. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, Allah has forgiven you. And he spoke good words to the one who helped her. Umar said: Stone the one who confessed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, he has repented to Allah. Ibn Umayr said, adding in it: Had the people of Madinah - or the people of Yathrib - repented it, it would have been accepted from them. So he released them."
"858","Ibn al-Muqri and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to cut for a quarter dinar and above."
"859","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut for a shield worth three dirhams."
"860","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Rafi ibn Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for fruit nor for palm-pith."
"861","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith and Hisham ibn Sad informed me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man of Muzaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think concerning sheep grazing on the mountain? He said: It and its like, and exemplary punishment; there is no cutting in anything of livestock except what the pen shelters, reaching the price of a shield, for in it is cutting of the hand; what does not reach the price of a shield, in it is a fine of twice its value and lashes as exemplary punishment. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think concerning hanging fruit? So he said: It and twice its value with it, and exemplary punishment; and there is no cutting in anything of fruit except what the threshing floor shelters; what is taken from the threshing floor reaching the price of a shield, in it is cutting; and what does not reach the price of a shield, in it is a fine of its like and lashes as exemplary punishment."
"862","Muhammad ibn Yahya, Harun ibn Ishaq, and Abu Zurah al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Asbat, from Simak, from Humayd, nephew of Safwan ibn Umayyah, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: I was sleeping in the mosque - and Harun said: sitting in the mosque - upon a cloak worth thirty dirhams. Then a man came and snatched it from me. So the man was seized and brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered him cut. So I came to him and said: Do you cut him for thirty dirhams? I sell it to him and defer its price. He said: Why was that not before you brought him to me?"
"863","Abu Jafar al-Mukharrimi Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk wine. He said: So he struck him with two palm stalks with him, about forty times. Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) did the like of that. When it was Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he consulted the people, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The lightest of the prescribed penalties is eighty."
"864","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Shabbabah informed us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk wine, so he struck him with two palm stalks forty times. And Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) did that. When it was Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he consulted the people, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to him: The lightest of the prescribed penalties is eighty, so he did it."
"865","897 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith - meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman - from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he becomes drunk, flog him, three times, then he said on the fourth: then strike his neck."
"866","898 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from Masruq, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three persons: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"867","899 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Qurra - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to us, from Muhammad - he is Ibn Sirin - who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra informed me, from his father; and 900 - Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice and said: What day is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Then he fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name, then he said: Is it not the town? We said: Yes indeed. He said: Allah has made sacred for you your blood and your wealth, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this town of yours, until the Day you meet your Lord. Have I not conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Let the one present convey to the one absent, for perhaps the one conveyed to retains better than the hearer. Beware, do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"868","901 - Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, who said: Mujahid narrated to us, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a slain person from among the people of the dhimma will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is found from such-and-such a distance, according to what its conveyor Marwan mentioned."
"869","902 - Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid - meaning Ibn Harun - narrated to us, he said: Uyayna ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from his father, from Abu Bakra, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a muahid without its due right, Allah forbids him Paradise, even to smell its scent."
"870","903 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, who said: I was with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was besieged in the house, and in the house there was an entrance; whoever entered it could hear the speech of those on the open courtyard. Uthman entered that entrance, then came out with his color changed, and said: They have just been threatening me with killing. We said: Allah will suffice you against them, O Commander of the Believers. He said: Why would they kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after his chastity, or kills a soul. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam at all, nor did I wish to exchange my religion since Allah guided me to it, nor did I kill a soul. So for what would they kill me?"
"871","904 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: that a Jew crushed the head of a slave-girl with a stone, then took silver ornaments that were on her. They found her while life remained in her, and they went around with her asking: Is it this one? Is it this one? Until she pointed to the Jew. They seized him and he confessed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning him and his head was crushed with stones."
"872","905 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatada informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: that a Jew crushed the head of a slave-girl between two stones. It was said to her: Who did this to you? Is it so-and-so or so-and-so? Until the Jew was named. He was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning him and his head was crushed with stones."
"873","906 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When you kill, do the killing well. Al-Ahmasi added: And when you slaughter, do the slaughter well."
"874","907 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed me - perhaps he said - from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from Hunnay ibn Nuwayra, from Alqama, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"875","908 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed me, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered retaliation for the tooth, and said: The Book of Allah is retaliation."
"876","909 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed me, from Firas, from Abu Salih, from Zadhan, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, when he called for a slave boy of his and freed him, then said: What reward do I have from him? What does this weigh - or what is this worth? And he took something from the ground in his hand. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever beats his slave for a prescribed punishment he did not incur, or slaps him, its expiation is to free him."
"877","910 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Aruba informed me, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"878","911 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed me, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Firas, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: Beware, I did not send my workers over you to strike your skins nor to take from your wealth; I only sent them to teach you your religion and your Sunna. Whoever has other than that done to him, let him raise it to me, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Umar, I will surely retaliate for him from him. Then Amr ibn al-As stood and said: O Commander of the Believers, if a Muslim man is over subjects and disciplines one of his subjects, will you retaliate from him? Umar said: How could I not retaliate from him, when I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) retaliate from himself? By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Umar, I will surely retaliate from him."
"879","912 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed me, he said: Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfa as a collector, and a man disputed with him over his charity dues, so Abu Jahm struck him and wounded his head. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Retaliation, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you is such-and-such. They were not pleased. He said: Then for you is such-and-such. They were not pleased. He said: Then for you is such-and-such. They were pleased. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am going to address the people and inform them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people and said: These Laythis came to me seeking retaliation, so I offered them such-and-such and they were pleased. Are you pleased? They said: No. The Emigrants moved toward them, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to hold back, so they held back. Then he called them and increased for them, and said: Are you pleased? They said: Yes. He said: Then I am going to address the people and inform them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people and said: Are you pleased? They said: Yes."
"880","913 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed me, from Qatada, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that a group from Ukl and Urayna professed Islam, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him they were people of udders and were not people of countryside, and they complained of the fever of Madina. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered for them some milch camels, and ordered for them a herdsman, and ordered them to go out and drink from their milk and urine. They set out toward al-Harra, then disbelieved after their Islam, killed the herdsman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and drove off the camels. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent searchers after them. They were brought, and he blinded their eyes, and cut off their hands and feet, and they were left toward al-Harra biting its stones until they died. Qatada said: It reached us that this verse was revealed about them: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger."
"881","914 - Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan ibn Abdullah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only blinded their eyes because they had blinded the eyes of the herdsmen."
"882","915 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us - and the hadith is that of Ibn al-Muqri - they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife has given birth to a black boy. He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there any gray among them? He said: There are gray ones among them. He said: Then how did that come to them? He said: Perhaps a strain pulled it. He said: And this one too, perhaps a strain pulled him."
"883","916 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Ghazwan informed me, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Abu al-Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Whoever slanders his slave while being unjust, the prescribed punishment will be carried out against him on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said."
"884","917 - al-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb - meaning Ibn al-Layth - informed me, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Abu Burda, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no flogging above ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from among the prescribed punishments of Allah."
"885","918 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Harun al-Burdi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Fayyad al-Abnawi, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that a man from Banu Bakr ibn Layth came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed that he had committed adultery with a woman four times, so he flogged him one hundred, as he was unmarried. Then he asked him for proof against the woman, so the woman said: He has lied, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. So he flogged him the prescribed punishment for slander, eighty."
"886","919 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yala narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he praised Allah and extolled Him, admonished and reminded, and said: To proceed, the prohibition of wine came down on the day it came down, and it is from five: from grapes, dates, wheat, barley, and honey. And wine is whatever covers the intellect."
"887","920 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When wine was prohibited we said: O Messenger of Allah, we have wine belonging to an orphan. So he ordered us and we poured it out."
"888","921 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Qabisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Hubayra, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wine being made into vinegar, and he disliked it."
"889","922 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."
"890","923 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Qurra, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have drinks - or a drink - from this bit made of honey, and mizr made of corn and barley; what do you command us? He said: I forbid you every intoxicant."
"891","924 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is unlawful."
"892","925 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - he is Ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping in the muqayyar, the muzaffat, the dubba, the hantama, and the naqir. He said: And every intoxicant is unlawful."
"893","926 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"894","927 - Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, he said: Abu Damra narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Bakr ibn Abi al-Furat, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"895","928 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed me, he said: Abu Uthman al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in the amount of a faraq, a handful of it is unlawful."
"896","929 - Sad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam and Allan ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed me, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I forbid you the small amount of whatever intoxicates in large amount."
"897","930 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them, for Muhammad was permitted to visit his mother, and it reminds of the Hereafter. And I forbade you keeping the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, intending thereby that the well-off widen upon those without means; so eat and store. And I forbade you vessels, though a vessel neither makes anything lawful nor unlawful. And every intoxicant is unlawful."
"898","931 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade unripe dates and ripe dates being mixed together, and raisins and dates being mixed together; and he wrote to the people of Jurash not to mix raisins and dates."
"899","932 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla; and Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla; and Abu Farwa, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: Hudhayfa, may Allah be pleased with him, asked for drink, so a dihqan brought him water in a silver vessel and he threw it aside, then excused himself to them for what he did and said: I had forbidden him; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not drink in vessels of gold and silver, nor wear dibaj nor silk; for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."
"900","933 - Abu Jafar al-Mukharrami, Ishaq ibn Mansur, and Umar ibn Shabba narrated to us - and the hadith is that of Abu Jafar - they said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shuba, who said: Qatada narrated to me, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man drinking while standing."
"901","934 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Hudayr informed me, from Yazid ibn Utarid Abu al-Bazari, who said: I asked Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, about drinking while standing, and he said: We used to drink while standing, and eat while walking, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"902","935 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik, from al-Bara ibn Zayd, son of the daughter of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that his mother reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her while a waterskin was hanging, and drank from the mouth of the skin standing. She said: So I stood to it and cut it off."
"903","936 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Qabisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from al-Qasim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat with his left hand, nor drink with his left hand; for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"904","937 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Umar ibn Muhammad, that Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed him that Salim ibn Abdullah informed him that Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this report. Abu Muhammad said: I heard Muhammad ibn Yahya say: al-Qasim in our view is Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, if Allah wills."
"905","938 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that dies in ghee. He said: If it is solid, throw it and what is around it away; and if it is liquid, do not approach it."
"906","939 - Ibn al-Muqri and Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratis narrated to us, they said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, may Allah be pleased with her: that a mouse fell into ghee and died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it and said: Throw it and what is around it away, and eat it."
"907","940 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a dead sheep belonging to one of his wives and said: Why did you not tan its hide and benefit from it?"
"908","941 - From Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata - and he had heard it forty years before - from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, may Allah be pleased with them."
"909","942 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Wala, from Ibn Abbas, raised - Ibn al-Muqri said: and once he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any hide that is tanned has become pure."
"910","943 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predators being spread as mats."
"911","944 - Muhammad Khalaf al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina while they were cutting off the humps of camels and the fat tails of sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion. Yahya ibn Main said: Yahya al-Qattan had narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar."
"912","945 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a woman who took a ring and filled it with the best of perfume, musk."
"913","946 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with Abu Ubayda on an expedition, and our provisions ran out. We passed by a whale cast up by the sea, and we wanted to eat from it, but Abu Ubayda forbade us. Then he said: We are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in the path of Allah, so eat. We ate from it for days. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we informed him, and he said: If anything of it remains with you, send some of it to us."
"914","947 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Hazim narrated to me, from Ibn Miqsam - Ahmad said: meaning Ubaydullah - from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about sea water and said: Its water is purifying, its dead is lawful."
"915","948 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyayna informed me, from Abu Yafur, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him. And Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Yafur, who said: I came to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about locusts? He said: We went on six expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eating locusts."
"916","949 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhadir narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Meat is brought to us and we do not know whether the name of Allah was mentioned over it or not. He said: Mention the name of Allah and eat."
"917","950 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The greatest of Muslims in crime against Muslims is one who asks about a matter that was not prohibited, then it is prohibited because of his question."
"918","951 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi and Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"919","952 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: On the day of Khaybar we slaughtered horses, mules, and donkeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us mules and donkeys, and did not forbid horses."
"920","953 - al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of donkeys, and permitted the meat of horses."
"921","954 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning Ibn Urwa - from Fatima, from Asma, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: We ate horse meat in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"922","955 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning al-Dastuwai - from Qatada, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah forbade the milk of the cow that eats filth, and the mujaththama, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"923","956 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, that a man avoided chicken, saying: I saw it eat something and found it repugnant. Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat it."
"924","957 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Thalaba al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every fanged beast of prey."
"925","958 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ammar, who said: I met Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said to him: Tell me about the hyena, do we eat it? He said: Yes. I said: Is it game? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"926","959 - Maruf ibn al-Hasan al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shuba, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, who said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, say: We flushed out a rabbit at Marr al-Zahran, and the people ran, and I caught it. I brought it to Abu Talha, who sent its thigh - he said: and I think he said: its haunch - to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he accepted it."
"927","960 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey, and every taloned bird."
"928","961 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey, and every taloned bird."
"929","962 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he was asked about eating lizards? He said: My maternal aunt Umm Hufayd gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ghee, dried curds, and lizards. He ate from the ghee and the dried curds, and left the lizards out of aversion to them. Had it been unlawful, it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor would he have ordered eating them."
"930","963 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri informed me, from his father, from Abaya ibn Rifaa, from Rafi ibn Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhu al-Hulayfa of Tihama, and the people seized sheep and camels, and hastened with them and boiled the pots. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon them and ordered the pots overturned, and equated ten sheep with a camel. He said: A camel among them bolted, and a man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These animals have wild strays like the strays of wild beasts; whatever overcomes you of them, do thus with it. He said: Then Rafi ibn Khadij came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we fear - or we hope - to meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives with us; shall we slaughter with reeds? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever causes blood to flow, with the name of Allah mentioned over it, eat, except the tooth and the nail. And I shall tell you: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of Abyssinia. Then he said: A water-carrying camel fell into a well in Madina and was slaughtered from the side of its flank, meaning its side, and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, took a tenth of it for two dirhams."
"931","964 - Ahmad ibn Said al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Hibban - meaning Ibn Hilal - narrated to us, he said: Jarir - meaning Ibn Hazim - narrated to us, he said: Ayyub used to narrate to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam; then I met Zayd and asked him, and he said: Ata ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man of the Ansar had a she-camel grazing toward Uhud, but it became refractory, so he slaughtered it with a stake. I said to Zayd: Of iron or of wood? He said: No, rather of wood. He said: Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about it, and he ordered him to eat it."
"932","965 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed me, he said: Yahya informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman used to graze sheep for Kab ibn Malik at Sal, and she feared a sheep would die, so she took a stone and slaughtered it with it. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered them to eat it."
"933","966 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us, from Shuba, he said: Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade animals being confined as targets."
"934","967 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has prescribed excellence upon everything; so do the killing excellently, and do the slaughtering excellently, and let one of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his slaughtered animal."
"935","968 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the fetus, and he said: Eat it if you wish, for its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."
"936","969 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - informed me, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Ushara, from his father: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughter only in the throat and the chest? He said: Had you stabbed it in its thigh it would have sufficed you. Ibn Mahdi said: This is regarding what cannot be overpowered, resembling the fallen animal."
"937","970 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqba - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams."
"938","971 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice cows on behalf of his wives."
"939","972 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Shababa narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter except a musinna, unless it is difficult for you, then slaughter a jadhaa of sheep."
"940","973 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, that Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani narrated to him, from Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a jadha of sheep."
"941","974 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed me. And Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Numan al-Hamdani, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said - and Ibn Hisham said, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us sacrificing a muqabala, a mudabara, a sharqa, a kharqa, or a jadaa."
"942","975 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed me, from Shuba, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman - freedman of Banu Asad - who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Fayruz - a man of Banu Shayban - say: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dislike among sacrifices, or what did he forbid? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four do not suffice - and my hand is shorter than his: the one-eyed whose blindness is clear, the lame whose lameness is clear, the sick whose sickness is clear, and the broken-boned that has no marrow. I said: I dislike any defect in the tooth, or in the horn, or any defect in the ear? He said: Whatever you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone."
"943","976 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Ali informed me, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none slaughter before praying. My maternal uncle Abu Burda ibn Niyar stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is abundant, and I slaughtered my sacrifice so my family and neighbors may eat from it, and I have a young goat better than two meat sheep; shall I slaughter it? He said: Yes, but no jadhaa will suffice for anyone after you, and it is the better of your two sacrifices."
"944","977 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed me, from Shuba, from Qatada, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say - so I said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes - The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two black-and-white horned rams, pronouncing the name and the takbir; I saw them both as he slaughtered them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
"945","978 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqa; it is slaughtered for him on the seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named."
"946","979 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Qasabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqa for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, a ram each."
"947","980 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqa for al-Hasan with a ram and for al-Husayn with a ram. 981 - al-Thawri, Ibn Uyayna, Hammad ibn Zayd and others narrated it from Ayyub, not going beyond Ikrima with it."
"948","982 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No fara and no atira."
"949","983 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym and Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim - Ibn Yahya said: and this is the hadith of Abu Nuaym - who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad? He said: What strikes with its edge, eat; and what strikes with its side is waqidh. He said: And I asked him about hunting with dogs. He said: What it holds for you, eat, for the taking of the dog is its slaughter. If you find with your dog another dog or other dogs, and fear it may have taken it with it and killed it, do not eat, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention it over the other."
"950","984 - Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Bayan Abu Bishr narrated to me, from Amir al-Shabi, who said: Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, we send trained dogs and they kill. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When they kill, eat, unless it eats from it, or another dog joins it."
"951","985 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Rabia ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Abu Thalaba al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of People of the Book and eat in their vessels, and we are in a land of hunting, so I shoot with my bow, and hunt with my trained dog and my untrained dog. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are in a land of People of the Book as you mentioned, do not eat in their vessels, unless you find no alternative; if you find no alternative, wash them then eat in them. And if you are in a land of hunting as you mentioned, what you hunt with your bow, mention the name of Allah and eat; what you hunt with your trained dog, mention the name of Allah and eat; and what you hunt with your untrained dog, if you reach its slaughter in time, eat."
"952","986 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, that he heard Rabia ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi say: I heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani say: He heard Abu Thalaba al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the story of the dog alone. And he said at its end: And whatever you do not reach in time for its slaughter, do not eat, in the story of the untrained dog."
"953","987 - Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, who said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the mirad. He said: If it pierces, eat; if it strikes with its side, do not eat."
"954","988 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us, from Shuba, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek its trail after a night, and find my arrow in it. He said: If you find it with your arrow in it and no beast has eaten from it, eat."
"955","989 - He said: I mentioned it to Abu Bishr, and he said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you find your arrow in it and see no trace in it from other than it, knowing that it killed it, eat."
"956","990 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Abi Zaida - narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If your shot falls into water and it drowns, do not eat."
"957","991 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek the trail after a night. He said: If you find your arrow in it and no beast has eaten from it, eat."
"958","992 - Shuba said: I mentioned it to Abu Bishr and he narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you find your arrow in it and see no trace in it from other than it, knowing that it killed it, eat."
"959","993 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say: By my father! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you swearing by your fathers. He said: By Allah, I never swore by him after that, neither deliberately nor quoting. The hadith is that of Ibn al-Muqri."
"960","994 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed me, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by the taghuts."
"961","995 - Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Khasib and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam is as he said. And he was among those who pledged allegiance under the tree."
"962","996 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding the word of Allah Almighty: Allah does not hold you accountable for idle talk in your oaths: she said: It was revealed concerning a man saying: Yes, by Allah, and No, by Allah."
"963","997 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath by which he seizes the wealth of a Muslim man, lying therein, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. Then there came down: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. Then al-Ash'ath ibn Qays entered and said: What is Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating to you? We said: Such and such. He said: He spoke the truth; it was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man of my people over some land of ours, so I brought him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Your proof. And I had no proof, so he said to him: Swear. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath by which he seizes the wealth of a Muslim man, lying therein, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. Then there came down: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, the verse."
"964","998 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nistas informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man swears a sinful oath at this pulpit of mine, even over a green tooth-stick, except that he takes his seat in the Fire."
"965","999 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then says: If Allah wills, has made an exception."
"966","1000 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath."
"967","1001 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you persists in his oath concerning his family, it is more sinful for him before Allah than the expiation He commanded."
"968","1002 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from a man of the Ansar, that he came with a black slave-girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave, so if you consider this one a believer I shall free her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you believe in resurrection after death? She said: Yes. He said: Then free her."
"969","1003 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow brings the son of Adam nothing I had not decreed for him; rather the vow meets what I had decreed for him. I extract thereby from the miser; he gives Me thereby what he would not have given Me before."
"970","1004 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Thaqif were allies of Banu Uqayl, and Thaqif captured two men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) captured a man of Banu Uqayl and seized with him al-Adba'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was in bonds, and he said: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! So he came to him and said: What is your concern? He said: Why did you seize me, and why did you seize the vanguard of the pilgrims? He said, magnifying that. He said: I seized you for the crime of your allies, Thaqif. Then he turned away from him, and he called out to him: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! And the Messenger of Allah was merciful and gentle, so he returned to him and said: What is your concern? He said: I am a Muslim. He said: Had you said it while you controlled your own affair, you would have prospered fully. Then he turned away from him, and he called out to him: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! So he came to him and said: What is your concern? He said: I am hungry, so feed me, and thirsty, so give me drink. He said: This is your need. He said: So he was ransomed in exchange for the two men. And a woman of the Ansar was captured, and al-Adba' was seized. The woman was in bonds, and the people used to graze their livestock in front of their houses. One night she slipped out of her bonds and came to the camels; whenever she approached a camel it growled, so she left it, until she reached al-Adba', which did not growl. It was a trained she-camel, so she mounted its rump, then urged it on and it set off. They were alerted about her, pursued her, but she eluded them. He said: And she had vowed that if Allah saved her, she would slaughter it. When she reached Madinah, the people saw it and said: Al-Adba', the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: She vowed that if Allah saved her, she would slaughter it. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Glory be to Allah! What an evil reward she gave her: that since Allah saved her, she would slaughter it? There is no fulfillment in disobedience of Allah, nor in what the servant does not own."
"971","1005 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah informed us. And Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Him, let him not disobey Him."
"972","1006 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Vows are of two kinds: what is for Allah, its expiation is fulfillment; and what is for Satan, there is no fulfillment in it, and upon him is the expiation of an oath."
"973","1007 - Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his sister, who vowed to walk to the Ka'bah, and he said: Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial animal. 1008 - And Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated it from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, without mentioning: let her offer a sacrificial animal."
"974","1009 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, that his sister vowed to walk to the House, so he sought a ruling for her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command her to ride. And Abu al-Khayr used to keep close to Uqbah."
"975","1010 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to me, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, there was a man standing in the sun. He asked about him, and they said: This is Abu Isra'il; he vowed to stand and not sit, not seek shade, not speak, and to fast. He said: Command him to speak, seek shade, sit, and complete his fast."
"976","1011 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons, and said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk to the House. He said: Allah is in no need of this one's tormenting himself. So he ordered him to ride."
"977","1012 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sa'd, that he said: My mother died with a vow upon her, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to fulfill it on her behalf."
"978","1013 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in the Days of Ignorance to spend a night in retreat in the Sacred Mosque. He said to him: Fulfill your vow."
"979","1014 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, Muslim al-Batin, and Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, Mujahid, and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister died with two consecutive months of fasting upon her. He said: If your sister owed a debt, would you pay it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the right of Allah is more deserving."
"980","1015 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, that Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to him, from Urwah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies with fasting upon him, his guardian fasts on his behalf."
"981","1016 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, informed us, from Shu'bah, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to perform pilgrimage, and she died. He said: If she owed a debt, would you pay it? He said: Yes. He said: Then pay Allah, for He is most deserving of fulfillment."
"982","1017 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray here, meaning in the Sacred Mosque. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Pray here."
"983","1018 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not right for a Muslim man who spends two nights with something to bequeath concerning, except that his will is written with him."
"984","1019 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I fell ill in Makkah with an illness from which I nearly died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and none inherits from me except my daughter; shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: No. I said: Then half? He said: No. I said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs rich, it is better than leaving them dependent."
"985","1020 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, owning no wealth besides them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them, divided them into thirds, cast lots among them, freed two and kept four enslaved. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke stern words to him."
"986","1021 - Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, and Salim ibn Amir and others narrated to me, from Abu Umamah and others who witnessed the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day. Among what he said was: Indeed Allah has given every rightful one his right; there is no bequest for an heir."
"987","1022 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger judged debts before bequests, though you recite: after any bequest he bequeaths or debt. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged inheritance for full brothers, to the exclusion of half-brothers through the father."
"988","1023 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj and Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Abadah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding His word: And whoever is poor, let him eat honorably. He said: It was revealed concerning the guardian of the orphan who manages him and stands over him: if he is needy, he may eat from it."
"989","1024 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am poor, I own nothing, and I have an orphan. He said: Eat from your orphan's wealth without extravagance, wastefulness, or hoarding."
"990","1025 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding: To all We appointed heirs. He said: Heirs. And regarding: As for those with whom you made pledges, give them their share. He said: When the Emigrants came to Madinah, an Emigrant used to inherit from an Ansari to the exclusion of his blood relatives, through the brotherhood the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had established between them. When the verse came down: To all We appointed heirs, it abrogated it. Then he recited: As for those with whom you made pledges, give them their share: of help, counsel, support, and bequest; the inheritance has gone."
"991","1026 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever from the Muslim."
"992","1027 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us. And Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Attach the fixed shares to their rightful owners; what remains belongs to the nearest male relative."
"993","1028 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me, he and Abu Bakr, among Banu Salimah. He found me unconscious, so he called for water, performed ablution, and sprinkled some of it over me. I came to, and said: How should I dispose of my wealth, O Messenger of Allah? Then there came down: Allah instructs you concerning your children: for the male twice the share of the female."
"994","1029 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever leaves wealth, it belongs to his agnates; and whoever leaves a burden or dependents, they come to me, for I am his guardian."
"995","1030 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me, he and Abu Bakr, both walking, while I had lost consciousness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution then poured his ablution water over me. I came to and said: O Messenger of Allah, how should I settle my wealth? How should I dispose of my wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer me, until the inheritance verse came down. 1031 - He said: And Abu al-Zubayr said: There came down concerning him: They ask you; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah."
"996","1032 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Kharashah, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abu Bakr asking him for her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I know nothing for you in the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); go back until I ask the people. So he asked the people, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give her a sixth. Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone with you besides you? Then Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughirah had said, so Abu Bakr granted it to her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, asking him for her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the judgment that reached us which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave was for other than you. I shall not add anything to the fixed shares; but it is that sixth: if you both share it, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"997","1033 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Abu al-Munib informed us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted the grandmother a sixth, when there is no mother."
"998","1034 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son died; what of his inheritance is mine? He said: A sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him and said: Another sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him and said: The other sixth is a bonus. Qatadah said: The least the grandfather inherits is a sixth, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him a sixth; and we do not know with whom he made him inherit."
"999","1035 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a man who left his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister: he gave his daughter half, his son's daughter a sixth, and the rest to his sister."
"1000","1036 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Shumayl, narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim; al-Aswad said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal judged among us in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a man who left his daughter and his sister. He said: He judged half for his daughter and half for his sister."
"1001","1037 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah: Teach your boys swimming and your fighters archery. They used to compete at targets, when a stray arrow came and killed a boy in the care of a maternal uncle of his, of unknown origin. Abu Ubaydah wrote to Umar: To whom shall I hand his blood-money? Umar wrote, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of whoever has no guardian, and the maternal uncle is the heir of whoever has no heir."
"1002","1038 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam al-Kindi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves a debt or dependents, they come to me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of whoever has no guardian: I inherit his wealth and ransom his captive. And the maternal uncle is the guardian of whoever has no guardian: he inherits his wealth and ransoms his captive."
"1003","1039 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Blood-money belongs to the paternal kin, and a wife does not inherit from her husband's blood-money, until al-Dahhak al-Kilabi informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to him to grant the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi her share of her husband's blood-money."
"1004","1040 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih informed us, from Umar ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, who said: My father informed me, from my grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: People of two religions do not inherit from one another. A wife inherits from her husband's blood-money and wealth, and he inherits from her blood-money and wealth, unless one of them kills the other. If one of them kills the other, he inherits nothing of his blood-money or wealth; and if one of them kills the other by mistake, he inherits from his wealth but not from his blood-money."
"1005","1041 - Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Makki, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from Sa'id ibn Marjanah, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believing slave, Allah frees for every limb of his a limb from the Fire, so that He frees the hand for the hand, the leg for the leg, and the private part for the private part. Ali ibn Husayn said: O Sa'id, did you hear this from Abu Hurayrah? He said: Yes. Thereupon Ali ibn Husayn said to a slave of his, the chief of his slaves: Call Mutarrif to me. When he came before him, he said: Go, you are free for the sake of Allah."
"1006","1042 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, that is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Hisham, who said: My father informed me, that Abu Mirwah al-Ghifari informed him, that Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah and struggle in His path. He said: Which slaves are best? He said: The most expensive and most precious to their owners. I said: What if I do not do that? He said: Help one who cannot earn, or make for one who cannot craft. I said: What if I am too weak for that? He said: Refrain from evil, for it is charity you give to yourself."
"1007","1043 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If a slave is owned by partners and one of them frees his share, he must free the rest of him, if he has enough wealth for that; otherwise, what was freed of him is freed."
"1008","1044 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd and Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child can repay his father, except to find him enslaved, buy him, and free him."
"1009","1045 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Damrah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a blood relative whom it is unlawful to marry is free."
"1010","1046 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet said: Whoever owns a blood relative whom it is unlawful to marry is free."
"1011","1047 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Harith, from Abu Zur'ah, who said: Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I shall always love Banu Tamim after three things I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard him say: They are the fiercest of my community against the Dajjal. And their charities came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the charities of our people. And Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, had a captive woman of them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free her, for she is of the children of Isma'il."
"1012","1048 - Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"1013","1049 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Jumhan informed us, he said: Safinah Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Umm Salamah freed me, stipulating upon me that I serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as he lived."
"1014","1050 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Shu'bah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Barirah, whose family had stipulated the right of clientage, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage belongs only to the one who frees."
"1015","1051 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar, the freedman of Ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of clientage and its gifting."
"1016","1052 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Ibn Ajlan, who said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three, all of whom Allah is bound to help: the fighter in the path of Allah, the one who marries to remain chaste, and the contracted slave who seeks to pay."
"1017","1053 - And Ibn Hashim narrated to us another time, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"1018","1054 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abadah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Barirah came to me and said: My family contracted me for nine ounces over nine years, an ounce each year, so help me. She said: I said: If your family wish that I count it out to them in one sum and free you, I shall do so, on condition my clientage over you remains. She went to her family and spoke to them about that, but they refused unless clientage belonged to them. She came to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and told her what her family had said. Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Then no. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her about that, and she told him what they had said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah: Buy her and free her, stipulating clientage for them, for clientage belongs only to the one who frees. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people; he praised Allah and glorified Him, then said: What is with men among you who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Any condition not in the Book of Allah is void, even if a hundred conditions. The decree of Allah is most true, and the condition of Allah is most binding. What is with men among you, one of whom says: Free so-and-so, but clientage belongs to me? Clientage belongs only to the one who frees."
"1019","1055 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a contracted slave, when killed, that blood-money is paid for him according to how much of him was freed, the blood-money of a free man. And Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: Upon a contracted slave is imposed only the punishment of a slave."
"1020","1056 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man of the Ansar granted a slave of his deferred freedom, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold him."
"1021","1057 - al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: A man freed a slave of his in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), owning no wealth besides him, as deferred freedom after his death. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Who will buy him from me? Nu'aym ibn Abdullah said: I shall buy him, and bought him. Amr said: Jabir said: A Coptic slave, who died the previous year. 1058 - Ibn Jurayj said: And Abu al-Zubayr added in it: called Ya'qub."
"1022","1059 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Life-grants are inheritance for their recipients, or lawful for their recipients."
"1023","1060 - Ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"1024","1061 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man is granted a life-grant for himself and his offspring, it belongs to the one given it; it does not return to the one who gave it, for he gave a gift in which inheritance takes effect."
"1025","1062 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The life-grant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted is for one to say: It is yours and your offspring's. But if he says: It is yours as long as you live, it returns to its owner. Ma'mar said: And al-Zuhri used to give ruling by it."
"1026","1063 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch-grants belong to whoever is watched with them, and life-grants to whoever is granted them for life."
"1027","1064 - Hasan ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no watch-grant and no life-grant. Whoever is granted something for life or watched with it, is granted something or watched with it, it is his in his life and after his death. He said: Watch-grant is for one to say to the other: It is between me and you. And life-grant is to grant him his life, that he make him live it out their lives. Ata said: If he gives him a year or two years or something he names, it is a temporary grant he grants him; it is not a life-grant."
"1028","1065 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: My father Bashir ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness a gift he had given me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you give all your children the like of this? He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"1029","1066 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: My father set out with me, carrying me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having given me a gift, to witness him to it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given al-Nu'man this slave boy as a gift; bear witness to it. He said: Did you give all your children the like of this? He said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would you like them to be equal toward you in dutifulness? He said: Yes. He said: Then have someone else witness this."
"1030","1067 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"1031","1068 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us. And Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. And the likeness of one who gives a gift then takes it back is like a dog that ate until, when sated, it vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"1032","1069 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father wants to seize my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. The best of what you eat is from your earnings, and the wealth of your children is from your earnings, so eat it with wholesome enjoyment."
"1033","1070 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me between sunset and night prayer by lamplight on the farewell night. He said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the judge strives and is correct, he has two rewards; and if he strives and errs, he has one reward."
"1034","1071 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A judge shall not judge between two men while angry."
"1035","1072 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ask for leadership; if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, and if you are given it through asking, you will be left to it."
"1036","1073 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us. And Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abadah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You bring your disputes to me, and I am only human; perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another. If I judge for one of you something of his brother's right, I am only cutting for him a piece of the Fire, so let him take nothing of it."
"1037","1074 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to us, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Two men of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing over inheritances between them long effaced, with no proof between them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You bring your disputes to me, and I am only human; perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another. I judge between you only by what I hear from you. Whoever I judge for him something of his brother's, let him not take it, for I am only cutting for him a piece of the Fire; he will come with it as a yoke on his neck on the Day of Resurrection. The two men wept, and each said: My right belongs to my brother. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Since you have done this, go, divide it, seek the truth, cast lots, then let each of you absolve the other."
"1038","1075 - Abu Salih Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Hamzah, narrated to me, from Kathir, meaning Ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muslims are bound by their conditions, whatever of them agrees with the truth."
"1039","1076 - And that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Settlement is lawful among Muslims."
"1040","1077 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever innovates in this affair of ours what is not in it is rejected."
"1041","1078 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained a man on suspicion, then released him."
"1042","1079 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from his father Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when two men came disputing over land. One of them said: This one seized my land, O Messenger of Allah, in the Days of Ignorance, and he is Imru' al-Qays ibn Abis al-Kindi, his opponent being Rabi'ah ibn Aydan. He said to him: Your proof. He said: I have none. He said: His oath. He said: Then he will take it. He said: You have nothing but that. When he stood to swear, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes land wrongfully will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."
"1043","1080 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Sulayman al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Kurdus narrated to me, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man of Kindah and a man of Hadramawt disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land in Yemen. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah! My land; his father seized it from me. He said to the Kindi: What do you say? He said: I say: It is land in my possession, inherited from my father. He said to the Hadrami: Do you have proof? He said: No, but let him swear, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah besides whom there is no god, that he does not know it is my land his father seized from me. The Kindi prepared to swear, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No man seizes wealth by his oath except that he meets Allah on the Day of Resurrection leprous. So the Kindi returned it."
"1044","1081 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani and Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratis narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with one witness and an oath. 1082 - Ahmad ibn Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abdullah, who said: I asked Yahya ibn Sa'id about Sayf ibn Sulayman, and he said: He was with us firm, truthful and retentive."
"1045","1083 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, from Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, from Rabi'ah, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath alongside a single witness."
"1046","1084 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath alongside a witness."
"1047","1085 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The testimony of a Bedouin against a townsman is not permitted."
"1048","1086 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, who said: Uqbah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, then said: He did not narrate to me, but I heard him narrating. He said: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, when a black woman came and said: I suckled you both. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he turned away from me. Then I asked him, and he turned away from me. Then he said at the fourth or third time: How can you keep her, when it has been said? He said: So he forbade him from her."
"1049","1087 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, who said: And Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: I also heard from Uqbah. He said: I married a woman in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: A black woman came and claimed she had suckled them both. He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, saying: She is lying. He turned away from me. Then I moved to the other side and said: O Messenger of Allah, she is lying. He said: What will you do with this one's word? Leave her. Ma'mar said: And I heard Ayyub say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can you keep her, when it has been said?"
"1050","1088 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the oath to a people, and both parties hastened to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered lots to be cast between them as to the oath, which of them would swear."
"1051","1089 - Ibn al-Muqri and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned the Ansar to grant them Bahrain, but they said: Not until you grant our brothers of the Emigrants. He said: You will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me."
"1052","1090 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Urwah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives land belonging to no one is most entitled to it. Urwah said: And Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, judged by that in his caliphate."
"1053","1091 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around land, it is his."
"1054","1092 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no reserve except for Allah and His Messenger."
"1055","1093 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Abu Awanah and Abd al-Aziz ibn Mukhtar informed us, both from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Yusuf, the nephew of Ibn Sirin, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If you differ over a road, its width is seven cubits."
"1056","1094 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id al-Duba'i, from Qatadah, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b al-Adawi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the road seven cubits."
"1057","1095 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever steals any part of land will have it hung around his neck from seven earths."
"1058","1096 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you whose neighbour asks his permission to fix his timber in his wall asks him, let him not prevent him. When Abu Hurayrah finished his hadith they lowered their heads, and he said: Why do I see you turning away from it?! By Allah, I shall surely cast it between your shoulders."
"1059","1097 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid and al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him), that he brought a dispute with a man of the Ansar who had been present at Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a water-channel from the lava field with which both of them watered their date-palms. The Ansari said: Let the water flow through. He refused him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then send the water on to your neighbour. The Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is your aunt's son? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed colour, then he said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then hold back the water until it returns to the embankment. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thus claimed the full right of al-Zubayr. Before that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had suggested to al-Zubayr a view intended to accommodate both al-Zubayr and the Ansari. Al-Zubayr said: I do not think this verse came down except concerning that: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what arises between them. One of the two narrators adds to the other in the story."
"1060","1098 - Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Qazzaz al-Dari narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud Umar ibn Sa'd al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: One of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) presented food to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a bowl, so A'ishah struck the bowl with her hand and dropped it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Food for food and a vessel for a vessel."
"1061","1099 - Bahr ibn Nasr informed us that Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to them, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani, who said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the Farewell Pilgrimage: A borrowed item is to be returned, a granted milch-animal is to be given back, a debt is to be paid off, and a guarantor is liable."
"1062","1100 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is liable for what it takes until it delivers it."
"1063","1101 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Hind bint Utbah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man and does not give me and my child what suffices us except what I take from his wealth without his knowledge. He said: Take what suffices you and your child in a customary manner."
"1064","1102 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever recognises his goods in the possession of a man takes them from him, and the one who had bought them seeks recompense from the one he bought them from."
"1065","1103 - Ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith and al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Iyad ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man suffered a loss in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in fruits he had bought, and his debt grew large. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity to him. So charity was given to him but it did not cover his debt. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his creditors: Take what you find, and you have nothing but that."
"1066","1104 - Abu Qilabah al-Raqqashi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Majid, that is Ibn Abi Yazid, Abu Wahb, narrated to me, he said: al-Ad'da' ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah said to me: Shall I not read to you a document the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me? I said: Yes indeed. He brought out a document for me, and in it was: This is what al-Ad'da' ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah bought from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): a slave, male or female - Abbad doubts - with no disease, no fraud and no hidden defect; the sale of one Muslim to another Muslim."
"1067","Chapter on emigration, 1105 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about emigration. He said: Woe to you, emigration is a grave matter. Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: Do you pay their charity? He said: Yes. He said: Do you grant some of them for use? He said: Yes. He said: Do you milk them for others on the day they are brought to water? He said: Yes. He said: Then work beyond the seas, for Allah will not diminish anything of your deeds."
"1068","1106 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the Conquest, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."
"1069","Chapter on the continuance of jihad until the Day of Resurrection, 1107 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A group of my community will continue fighting upon the truth, triumphant, until the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then Jesus son of Mary will descend, and their leader will say: Come, lead us in prayer. He will say: No; some of you are leaders over others, as an honour from Allah to this community."
"1070","Chapter concerning what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded of calling to the oneness of Allah and fighting for it, 1108 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Uthman, meaning Ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir, narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. Whoever says: There is no god but Allah has protected his life and his property from me except by its due right, and his reckoning is with Allah."
"1071","Chapter on jihad as a collective obligation, 1109 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my community - or he said: upon the people - I would love never to stay behind an expedition going forth, or setting out, in the path of Allah. But I do not find means to carry them, and they do not find means to follow me, and it is hard for them to stay behind after me. So I wish that I fight in the path of Allah and am killed, then am brought to life and am killed, then am brought to life and am killed."
"1072","Chapter on one who has an excuse for staying behind, 1110 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, who said: I saw Marwan ibn al-Hakam sitting in the mosque, so I came until I sat by him, and he informed us that Zayd ibn Thabit informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dictated to him: Not equal are those of the believers who sit and those who strive in the path of Allah. He said: Then Ibn Umm Maktum came to him while he was dictating it to me and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, if I could strive I would strive - and he was a blind man - so Allah sent down upon His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while his thigh was upon my thigh, and it grew heavy until I feared it would crush my thigh. Then he was relieved of it, and Allah sent down: Except those with a disability."
"1073","1111 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): A man emigrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have emigrated. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have abandoned idolatry, but it is striving in the path of Allah. Do you have anyone in Yemen? He said: My parents. He said: Did they permit you? He said: No. He said: Go back and seek their permission; if they permit you, then strive, otherwise be dutiful to them."
"1074","Chapter on the stern warning against abandoning campaigning, 1112 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Asad, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies without having campaigned, with no resolve to do so in himself, dies upon a branch of hypocrisy."
"1075","Chapter on what suffices of campaigning and on equipping a fighter, 1113 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a fighter in the path of Allah has himself fought, and whoever looks after a fighter's family well in his absence has himself fought."
"1076","1114 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sa'id the freedman of al-Mahri, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent troops to Banu Lihyan and said: Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is shared between them."
"1077","Chapter on payment for campaigning, 1115 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Kindi narrated to me, from Ibn Shufayy, from Shufayy, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A return from campaign is like a campaign. And he said: The fighter has his reward, and the one who pays for him has his own reward and the reward of the fighter."
"1078","Chapter on what is owed of obedience to commanders and of refusing them when they command disobedience, 1116 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ya'la ibn Muslim informed me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that he said: O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you - it was revealed concerning Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi al-Sahmi, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him out with an expedition."
"1079","1117 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearing and obeying are binding upon the Muslim man unless he is commanded to disobey Allah. When he is commanded to disobey, there is neither hearing nor obeying."
"1080","Chapter on the counsel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to armies and commanders, 1118 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, who narrated to him, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a commander over an army or an expedition, he would call him and counsel him regarding himself in particular and those Muslims with him with good. He would say: Campaign in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Campaign, and do not act treacherously, do not misappropriate spoils, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the polytheists, call them to one of three courses - or traits - and if they answer you to any of them, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them: Call them to Islam; if they do so, inform them that they have what the Muslims have and upon them is what is upon the Muslims. Then call them to move from their abode to the abode of the Emigrants; if they do so, inform them that they have what the Emigrants have and upon them is what is upon the Emigrants. If they accept Islam and choose their own abode, inform them that they are like the Bedouin believers, subject to the ruling of Allah that applies to the believers - or he said: the Muslims - and that they have no share in the spoils or the fay'. If they refuse, call them to pay the jizyah; if they do so, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them. If they refuse, seek Allah's help and fight them. When you besiege a fortress and they want you to grant them the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, do not grant them the covenant of Allah nor the covenant of His Messenger; grant them your own covenant and the covenant of your fathers and the covenants of your companions, for it is lighter for you to break your own covenant and the covenants of your fathers than to break the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger. And when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, for you do not know whether you will hit Allah's judgment concerning them; rather bring them down upon your own judgment."
"1081","Chapter on the prohibition of killing women and children, 1119 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) informed him: A woman was found slain in one of the campaigns of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) condemned the killing of women and children."
"1082","Chapter on the lifting of blame from one who hits them in a night raid, 1120 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was at al-Abwa' - or at Waddan - and he heard him asked about the enemy settlement that is attacked by night so that some of their women and offspring are struck. He said: They are of them."
"1083","Chapter on the age at which a boy leaves the category of offspring, 1121 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: On the day of Banu Qurayzah they would look at a man's pubic hair; if it had grown they killed him, and if it had not grown they spared him. They looked at my hair and it had not grown, so they spared me."
"1084","Chapter on the prohibition of killing envoys, 1122 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man - meaning the envoy of Musaylimah: Were it not that you are an envoy, I would have killed you."
"1085","Chapter on omitting the call to the polytheists before fighting, 1123 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh, meaning Ibn Mu'adh, narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, who said: I wrote to Nafi' asking him whether there had been a call before fighting. He wrote back to me: That was only at the beginning of Islam; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were heedless, with their cattle being watered at the water, so he killed them and took their captives. On that day he took Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated this to me, and he had been in that army."
"1086","Chapter on not seeking the aid of the polytheists, 1124 - Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tarsusi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): A man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was heading for Badr: Shall I go out with you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not seek the aid of a polytheist."
"1087","Chapter on the number from which flight is not permitted, 1125 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: It was prescribed upon them that one man should not flee from ten, and that twenty should not flee from two hundred. Then it was lightened for them, and He said: Now Allah has lightened for you. And it was prescribed upon them that one hundred should not flee from two hundred, nor ten from twenty."
"1088","Chapter explaining flight from the battle line to a supporting force, 1126 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition; the people swerved aside in retreat, and we entered Medina and hid in the houses. Then we appeared before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are ruined, O Messenger of Allah; we are the deserters. He said: Rather you are those who return to fight; I am your supporting force."
"1089","Chapter on the concession for dissembling speech in war, 1127 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception."
"1090","Chapter on whose guarantee of safety is valid, and on returning detachments to the main army, 1128 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca in the year of the Conquest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as a preacher and said: O people, whatever alliance there was in the pre-Islamic age, Islam has only strengthened it; there is no alliance in Islam. The Muslims are one hand against others besides them; the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf, the furthest of them returns spoils to them, their detachments return to those who stayed behind, a believer is not killed for a disbeliever, the blood-money of a disbeliever is half the blood-money of a believer, there is no bringing animals to be milked at the collector nor taking them away from him, and their charities are taken only in their own dwellings."
"1091","Chapter on the stern warning against the treacherous, 1129 - Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner will be raised for every treacherous one, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so. The wording of the hadith is that of Ibn Yahya; al-Za'farani did not mention: on the Day of Resurrection."
"1092","Chapter on burning date-palms, 1130 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned the date-palms of Banu al-Nadir."
"1093","Chapter on the guarantee of safety granted by women, 1131 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Murrah, that Umm Hani' granted protection to two of her in-laws, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We grant protection to whom you have granted protection, and we give safety to whom you have given safety."
"1094","1132 - Ibn al-Muqri' said: And Sufyan narrated it to us another time, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Murrah the freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani' (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned it."
"1095","Chapter on the prohibition of mutilation, 1133 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Hayyaj: that a boy - perhaps he said: I am Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Hayyaj: that a boy - perhaps he said to his father - ran away, so he vowed that if he got hold of him he would cut off a part of him. When he came back to him, he sent me to Imran ibn Husayn, so I asked him. Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever wishes to free his slave or to expiate his oath, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge us to give charity and forbade mutilation. 1134 - He said: So I went to Samurah, and he said the like of what Imran had said."
"1096","Chapter on the prohibition of burning living beings, 1135 - Bahr ibn Nasr al-Khawlani narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth, from his father, from Bukayr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and said: If you find so-and-so and so-and-so - two men of Quraysh - burn them both with fire. Then when we were about to set out the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, yet none punishes with fire but Allah; so if you find them both, kill them both."
"1097","Chapter on a spy who is captured and then accepts Islam, 1136 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from al-Furat ibn Hayyan - who had been a spy for Abu Sufyan and an ally - while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered him killed. He passed by a circle of the Ansar, and a man of them said: O Messenger of Allah, he says: I am a Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among you are men whom we entrust to their faith; among them is al-Furat ibn Hayyan."
"1098","Chapter on keeping horses tied for battle, 1137 - Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. And Ibn Yahya said: forever, until the Day of Resurrection."
"1099","Chapter on wearing armour, 1138 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid - if Allah wills - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail on the day of Uhud."
"1100","1139 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a prophet, once he has put on his armour, to lay it down until he fights."
"1101","Chapter on a man training his horse and the virtue of archery, 1140 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Bayruti informed us that his father informed him, he said: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: Abu Sallam narrated to me, he said: Khalid, that is Ibn Yazid, narrated to me, who said: I was an archer, and Uqbah al-Juhani would call me saying: Come out with us, O Khalid, to shoot. One day I was late for him, so he said: Come, let me tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, and let me say to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah admits three people to Paradise by a single arrow: its maker who seeks good in making it, the one who shoots it, and the one who hands the arrows to him. Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me than that you ride. There is no idle pastime except in three: a man training his horse, his playing with his wife, and his shooting with his bow and arrows. Whoever abandons archery after learning it out of disinterest in it, it is a blessing he has been ungrateful for."
"1102","Chapter on watchwords in war, 1141 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the enemy attacks you by night, your watchword is: Ha-Mim, they shall not be helped."
"1103","Chapter on the dislike of taking copies of the Qur'an into enemy land, 1142 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade travelling with the Qur'an to enemy land, fearing the enemy would seize it."
"1104","Chapter on supplication at the time of fighting, 1143 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub informed us, he said: Abu Hazim ibn Dinar informed me, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two supplications are not rejected - or he said: are never rejected - supplication at the call to prayer and at the moment of battle when men join one another in combat."
"1105","Chapter on drawing up ranks for fighting and dismounting, 1144 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara' say: So he dismounted and sought help - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he said: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib. Then he drew up his companions in ranks."
"1106","Chapter on the leader staying in the enemy's courtyard and after conquest, 1145 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overcame a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard for three days."
"1107","Chapter on property seized by the enemy then falling into Muslim hands, 1146 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: A horse belonging to Ibn Umar went astray and the enemy took it; then the Muslims prevailed over them and it was returned to him in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And a slave of his fled and joined the land of Byzantium; then the Muslims prevailed over them and Khalid ibn al-Walid returned him to him after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1108","Chapter on the dislike of marching in enemy lands before the treaty term expires, 1147 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrami narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, from Sulaym ibn Amir, who said: There was a treaty between Mu'awiyah and Byzantium. A man called Amr ibn Abasah came to him on his horse, declaring: Allah is Most Great; fidelity, no treachery. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever has a treaty between him and a people must neither tighten a knot nor loosen it until its term expires or he renounces it to them on equal terms. So Mu'awiyah turned back the armies."
"1109","Chapter on the inviolability of the blood of covenanted non-Muslims, 1148 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, he said: Uyaynah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted person unlawfully, Allah forbids him Paradise, even to smell its fragrance."
"1110","Chapter on the beginning of spoils being made lawful, 1149 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah said: Spoils were not made lawful for any dark-haired people before you; a fire would descend from heaven and consume them. He said: When the day of Badr came, the people hastened to take spoils, so Allah sent down: Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took."
"1111","Chapter on the permissibility of the enemy's food without division, 1150 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, who said: The people of the mosque sent me to Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa, so I asked him: Concerning the food of Khaybar, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a fifth of it? He said: No; it was too trifling for that. Any one of us would take from it what he needed."
"1112","Chapter on detachments returning spoils to the main army, 1151 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslims' blood is equal in value, the lowest of them strives to grant protection on their behalf, the furthest of them grants refuge on their behalf, they are one hand against others, the strong among them returns spoils to the weak, and their raiding parties return to those who stayed behind. A believer is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while his covenant lasts."
"1113","Chapter on granting extra shares to a detachment leaving the army, from the fifth, 1152 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Nafi' informed us, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition toward Najd, and from that expedition he sent a detachment in which Ibn Umar was. Ibn Umar reported that the shares of the expedition reached twelve camels each, and the members of the detachment in which Ibn Umar was were given an extra camel each besides that. So the members of the detachment received thirteen each, thirteen each, while the members of the main expedition received twelve, twelve."
"1114","Chapter: another case of preferment, 1153 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa' narrated to me, he said: My father (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatadah, and the best of our foot-soldiers is Salamah. Then he gave me two shares: the share of the horseman and the foot-soldier together."
"1115","Chapter on awarding the slayer the spoils of the slain, 1154 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas narrate, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abu Muhammad the freedman of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn. When we met, the Muslims wavered at first. He said: I saw a man of the polytheists overpowering a Muslim man. He said: I circled round him until I came to him from behind and struck him on the cord of his shoulder. He turned on me and embraced me with an embrace in which I felt the scent of death. Then death overtook him and he released me. I caught up with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: What is the matter with the people? He said: It is Allah's decree. He said: Then the people returned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and said: Whoever kills a slain man with proof thereof, his spoils are his. Abu Qatadah said: I stood and said: Who will bear witness for me? Then I sat down. Then he said again: Whoever kills a slain man with proof thereof, his spoils are his. He said: I stood and said: Who will bear witness for me? Then I sat down. Then he said it a third time, so I stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What is the matter with you, O Abu Qatadah? He said: I told him the story. A man among the people said: He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; the spoils of that slain man are with me, so compensate him for his due. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No, by Allah; he would not turn to a lion of Allah's lions fighting for Allah and His Messenger and then give you his spoils. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth; give them to him. So he gave them to me. He said: I sold the coat of mail and bought with its price a garden of date-palms among Banu Salamah; it was the first wealth I acquired in Islam. He said: And al-makhraf means date-palms."
"1116","1155 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i and Khalid ibn al-Walid (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the spoils of the slain."
"1117","Chapter on granting extra shares to detachments after the fifth, after they have taken spoils, 1156 - Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mushir narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he granted a fourth extra after the fifth."
"1118","1157 - Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us that his father informed him, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz said, he said: Makhul narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he granted a fourth extra at the outset and a third on the return."
"1119","Chapter on the stern warning against misappropriation and where the fifth is placed, 1158 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return my cloak, return my cloak. By Allah, if I had livestock as numerous as the trees of Tihamah I would divide them among you; you will not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar. Then he stood beside a camel and took a hair from its hump and said: O people, I have nothing of your fay' but even the like of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So render back the thread and the needle, for misappropriation will be disgrace, fire and shame for its owner on the Day of Resurrection. Then a man of the Ansar came with a ball of hair threads and said: O Messenger of Allah, I took these to stitch the worn saddle-blanket of my camel with. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for my share, it is yours. He said: Since it has come to this, I have no need of it."
"1120","1159 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid, that is al-Ahmar, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abu Amrah, a freedman of theirs, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed him that Abu Amrah, the freedman of Zayd ibn Khalid, informed him that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani mention that a Muslim man died at Khaybar, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he pray over him. He said: Pray over your companion. The people's faces changed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what was in them, he said: Your companion misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah. He said: So we searched his baggage and found beads of Jewish beads, by Allah not worth two dirhams."
"1121","Chapter on burning the baggage of the misappropriator and his punishment, 1160 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar struck the misappropriator with the whip, burned his baggage and withheld his share."
"1122","Chapter on hastening the division of spoils near the enemy, 1161 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dividing the spoils at al-Ji'ranah when a man stood and said: Be just, for you have not been just. He said: Woe to you; who will be just if I am not just? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: Leave him, for this one has companions - or: is among companions - who recite the Qur'an without it passing their throats; they pass out of religion as an arrow passes out of the game."
"1123","Chapter on the share of the horseman and the foot-soldier, 1162 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned to a man and his horse three shares: one share for him and two shares for his horse."
"1124","Chapter on giving a gratuity to a woman and a slave who attend battle, 1163 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Anas ibn Iyad informed me, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz: Najdah wrote to Abd Allah ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas wrote back to him: You wrote asking me whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to campaign with women. He did use to campaign with them; they would treat the sick and be given something from the spoils, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix any share for them."
"1125","1164 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, who said: Najdah wrote to Abbas asking him about things. He said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read his letter and when he wrote back to him. He said: And you asked about a woman and a slave, whether they had a fixed share when they attended battle. They had no fixed share except to be given something from the spoils of the people."
"1126","1165 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar while I was a slave, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, assign a share to me. He said: So he gave me a sword and said: Gird yourself with this, and he gave me some of the mean household goods."
"1127","Chapter proving that spoils belong to those present at the battle, 1166 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, that Anbasah ibn Sa'id informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Sa'id ibn al-As: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Aban ibn Sa'id ibn al-As with a detachment from Medina toward Najd. Then Aban and his companions came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar after he had conquered it, with the girths of their horses of palm fibre. Aban said: Apportion to me, O Messenger of Allah. Abu Hurayrah said: I said: Do not apportion to them, O Messenger of Allah. Aban said: Here you are, O hyrax come down from the top of a sheep. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit, O Aban. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not apportion to them. And it has been narrated that he gave Ja'far and his companions from Khaybar."
"1128","1167 - Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Qirati narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: So we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he conquered Khaybar, and he assigned shares to us - or he said: he gave us from it - and he apportioned nothing of it to anyone absent from the conquest of Khaybar except to those who had been present with him, except the people of our ship with Ja'far and his companions, to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned."
"1129","Chapter on taking ransom from captives, 1168 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to me, from his father Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the people of Mecca sent concerning the ransom of their captives, Zaynab the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent concerning the ransom of Abu al-As, sending with it a necklace of hers which Khadijah had given her to wear when she married Abu al-As. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he felt intense pity for her and said: If you deem it fit to release her captive to her and return to her what belongs to her, then do so? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they released him and returned to her what belonged to her."
"1130","Chapter on freeing captives without ransom, 1169 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Mut'im ibn Adi, Abu Jubayr, been alive speaking to me concerning these filthy ones - meaning the captives of Badr - I would have released them to him. 1170 - Sufyan said once: Muhammad ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Flag: report 1170 is fragmentary in the printed text.]"
"1131","Chapter on dividing conquered land, 1171 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Were it not for the last of the Muslims, I would not have taken any town without dividing it, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided Khaybar."
"1132","Chapter on freeing slaves of the polytheists who accept Islam, 1172 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Two slaves of the people of Mecca went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah before the truce and accepted Islam. Their masters among the people of Mecca sent concerning them: By Allah, O Muhammad, they did not come out to you out of desire for your religion; they came out only fleeing from slavery. Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; return them to them. He grew angry and said: I do not see you, O company of Quraysh, desisting until Allah sends against you one who will strike your necks for this religion. He refused to return them and said: They are Allah's freedmen."
"1133","Chapter on what is owed of justice by rulers, 1173 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is answerable for his flock. The ruler over the people is a shepherd over them and is answerable for them. A man is a shepherd over his household and is answerable for them. A woman is a shepherdess over her husband's house and is answerable for them. A slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is answerable for it. Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is answerable for his flock."
"1134","Chapter on relieving armies in turn, 1174 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that Abd Allah ibn Ka'b al-Ansari informed him that an army of the Ansar among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umar, you have neglected us and left us unguarded, and abandoned among us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded of relieving armies with one another in turn. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"1135","Chapter on the pledge of allegiance, 1175 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us; they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, who heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take the pledge from each of us to hear and obey, then say to him: As far as you are able."
"1136","Chapter mentioning what is taken without fighting, the fifth and select spoils, 1176 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spend on his family for a year from the wealth of Banu al-Nadir, which was of what Allah granted His Messenger of what the Muslims had not spurred horse or camel against. What remained he put into horses and weapons as equipment in the path of Allah."
"1137","1177 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar, Abu al-Yaman and Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us; they said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him that Fatimah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them) asking him for her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what Allah had granted His Messenger. Fatimah at that time was seeking the charity of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Medina and Fadak, and what remained of the fifth of Khaybar. A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eat from this wealth - meaning the wealth of Allah - they have no right to take more than their food. By Allah, I shall not change any of the charities of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the state they were in during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I shall act in them as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted."
"1138","1178 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi and Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us; they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Abu al-Ala' Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: We were sitting in al-Mirbad in Basra when a Bedouin came with a piece of leather or a scrap of a bag and said: This is a document the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me. Abu al-Ala' said: I took it and read it to the people, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh: If you establish prayer, give charity, and give from the spoils the fifth and the Prophet's share and the select portion, you are safe under Allah's covenant and the covenant of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything? He said: I heard him say: Fasting the month of patience, and fasting three days of every month, removes the rancour of the heart. He said: I said: Did you yourself hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Do you think I would lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then he took the document and went off withdrawing. The hadith is that of al-Ahmasi, and the wording is close."
"1139","Chapter on expelling the Jews, 1179 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Jews of al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled Banu al-Nadir and left Qurayzah, granting them favour, until Qurayzah fought after that. Then he killed their men and divided their women, children and wealth among the Muslims, except that some of them joined the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he granted them safety and they accepted Islam. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled all the Jews of Medina: Banu Qaynuqa', who are the people of Abd Allah ibn Salam, the Jews of Banu Harithah, and every Jew in Medina."
"1140","Chapter mentioning Khaybar, 1180 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) contracted with Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of dates or crops."
"1141","1181 - al-Rabi' informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, he said: Usamah informed me, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: When Khaybar was conquered, the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to leave them in it on condition they work for half of what comes out of it of dates and crops. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall leave you in it upon that as long as we wish. They remained in it thus during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). The dates were divided according to shares from half of Khaybar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take the fifth."
"1142","Chapter on expelling the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula, 1182 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them) say: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I shall surely expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until I leave none but a Muslim."
"1143","Chapter on the jizyah, 1183 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen and ordered him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' or tabi'ah, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir garments."
"1144","1184 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, who heard Bajalah say: I was a scribe for Jaz' ibn Mu'awiyah, and the letter of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reached us a year before his death: Kill every sorcerer, separate every Magian related by blood from his kinswoman as in the Book of Allah, prepare food and lay the sword upon your thigh. They ate without humming and cast down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had not taken jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had taken it from the Magians of Hajar."
"1145","1185 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: Hisham ibn Hakim (may Allah be pleased with him) entered upon Umayr al-Ansari in Syria, who was a governor for Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). He entered upon him and found with him people of the Nabataeans standing in the sun. He said: What is the matter with these? He said: I detained them for the jizyah. Hisham said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever torments people in this world, Allah will torment him in the Hereafter. So Umayr released them and let them go."
"1146","1186 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil and Ibn al-Tabba' narrated to us; they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two religions - and Ibn al-Tabba' said: two qiblahs - cannot both be right in one town, and no jizyah is due upon a Muslim."
"1147","Chapter proving the levying of land-tax on conquered land, 1187 - al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Adam, narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iraq will withhold its qafiz and its dirham, Syria will withhold its mudy and its dinar, Egypt will withhold its irdabb and its dinar, and you will return to where you began. He said it three times. The flesh and blood of Abu Hurayrah bear witness to that."
"1148","Chapter on gifts of the polytheists, 1188 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Tabuk until we reached Tabuk. Then the king of Aylah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and presented the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a white mule. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a cloak and wrote for them concerning their sea."
"1149","1189 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran informed us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, that he presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a she-camel - or he said: a gift - so he said to him: Have you accepted Islam? He said: No. He said: I have been forbidden the offerings of the polytheists. [Flag: parenthetical phrase about their gifts is an editorial insertion in one transmission.]"
"1150","Chapter on the purposes for which fay' wealth is disbursed, 1190 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray over a man with a debt. A dead man was brought, and he asked: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he prayed over him. He said: When Allah granted His Messenger conquests, he said: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"1151","1191 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: When anything came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would distribute it the same day. He would give a married man two shares and an unmarried man one share. He said: So I was called - and I used to be called before Ammar ibn Yasir - and I was called and he gave me two shares, for I had a family. Then Ammar was called after, and he gave him one share."
"1152","1192 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib informed him that Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib met and said: By Allah, if we sent these two lads - meaning himself and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas - to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would appoint them over these charities. He mentioned part of the hadith. He said: So we spoke to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you that you appoint us over these charities. He said: Charity is not fitting for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad; it is but the people's impurities. Call Mahmiyah ibn al-Jaz' for me - he was in charge of tithes - and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. They both came to him, and he said to Mahmiyah: Marry this lad to your daughter, for al-Fadl; so he married him to her. And he said to Abu Sufyan: Marry this lad to your daughter; so he married him to her. Then he said to Mahmiyah: Pay their bridal gifts from the fifth."
"1153","1193 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam informed us that Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to them, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that when Mu'awiyah came to Medina performing pilgrimage, Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) came to him. Mu'awiyah said to him: Your need, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said to him: My need is the stipend of the freedmen, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when anything came to him, begin with none before them."
